WEBVTT

1
00:01:01.406 --> 00:01:06.639
TIME OUT

2
00:01:51.489 --> 00:01:52.922
Hello, Muriel.

3
00:01:54.192 --> 00:01:56.023
Did you sleep well?

4
00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:01.062
Did Alice have a hard time
getting up?

5
00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:04.767
I'm OK.

6
00:02:05.103 --> 00:02:08.630
I have a meeting
on the other side of Marseille.

7
00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.332
I'm already late.

8
00:02:12.276 --> 00:02:14.710
Yeah, it will take all morning.

9
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.542
I don't know.

10
00:02:17.648 --> 00:02:21.243
I'll call you at 1:00.
Will you be at home?

11
00:02:23.688 --> 00:02:25.053
Well, OK.

12
00:02:25.857 --> 00:02:28.052
Later... I love you.

13
00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:55.004
Muriel, I lost track of time.
I was afraid you already left for school.

14
00:04:58.376 --> 00:05:00.367
Sure, it went well...

15
00:05:00.478 --> 00:05:04.642
But impossible deadlines...
I had to catch us up.

16
00:05:07.018 --> 00:05:09.077
What? Are you kidding?

17
00:05:12.323 --> 00:05:14.188
Don't make fun of me!

18
00:05:17.628 --> 00:05:19.755
Don't expect me to be perfect.

19
00:05:19.864 --> 00:05:22.992
I'm losing you...
I can't hearyou.

20
00:05:24.902 --> 00:05:26.369
That's better.

21
00:05:27.004 --> 00:05:28.869
My day isn't over.

22
00:05:28.973 --> 00:05:31.339
Still another client to see.

23
00:05:32.944 --> 00:05:35.640
This one won't be easy
to get rid of.

24
00:05:35.746 --> 00:05:39.341
We have a restructuring plan to organize.

25
00:05:40.651 --> 00:05:43.085
I hope it won't end too late.

26
00:05:43.187 --> 00:05:45.985
Don't count on me for dinner.

27
00:05:48.292 --> 00:05:50.954
Of course, I plan to come home.

28
00:05:51.062 --> 00:05:53.860
I'll call you around 6:00.

29
00:05:54.832 --> 00:05:57.027
I'll know more then. OK?

30
00:05:57.868 --> 00:05:59.165
I love you.

31
00:06:32.303 --> 00:06:36.296
And now fortoday's
stock exchange report...

32
00:06:59.597 --> 00:07:01.758
It didn't go well at all.

33
00:07:02.066 --> 00:07:06.366
It took three of us...
But we didn't convince him.

34
00:07:08.572 --> 00:07:13.407
Now we'll have dinnertogether.
Sort of an emergency unit.

35
00:07:14.412 --> 00:07:16.505
Sorry. Tonight is off.

36
00:07:20.551 --> 00:07:22.348
Tomorrow, I promise.

37
00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.059
I have to talk to you
about Switzerland.

38
00:07:33.164 --> 00:07:37.498
There's a big chance.
It just may work out.

39
00:07:40.971 --> 00:07:43.030
Nothing's certain.

40
00:07:44.475 --> 00:07:47.069
We'll talk this weekend. OK?

41
00:07:50.147 --> 00:07:52.615
I have to go. I love you.

42
00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:54.817
See you tomorrow.

43
00:08:52.243 --> 00:08:54.074
Daddy! Daddy!

44
00:08:54.178 --> 00:08:56.612
How are my little monsters?

45
00:08:58.649 --> 00:09:00.879
Hurry up for my school fair!

46
00:09:00.985 --> 00:09:04.011
Mom said
you wouldn't arrive on time.

47
00:09:04.121 --> 00:09:05.213
Really?

48
00:09:08.159 --> 00:09:09.649
You're back so early!

49
00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:13.287
I got off early
because of yesterday's hell.

50
00:09:13.397 --> 00:09:17.697
I left you a note
because we're on our way out.

51
00:09:18.502 --> 00:09:22.768
We're only three teachers forthat fair!
I've had it, I swear.

52
00:09:22.873 --> 00:09:26.604
Hurry up, Alice. Or we'll be late.

53
00:09:27.778 --> 00:09:29.439
Your car or mine?

54
00:09:29.547 --> 00:09:32.778
I'm dead tired.
I'll rest and join you later.

55
00:09:32.883 --> 00:09:35.147
Felix is counting on you.

56
00:09:35.252 --> 00:09:37.720
Sure. Just a little nap.

57
00:09:37.821 --> 00:09:38.913
Hey, Mom!

58
00:09:39.924 --> 00:09:40.982
Hi, son.

59
00:09:43.194 --> 00:09:45.719
Muriel says you might change jobs.

60
00:09:45.829 --> 00:09:49.560
I asked you to keep it to yourself.
But you had to tell her...

61
00:09:49.667 --> 00:09:52.363
- True orfalse?
- Nothing's sure yet.

62
00:09:52.469 --> 00:09:54.869
Good luck getting information
out of him!

63
00:09:54.972 --> 00:09:56.200
Grandma!

64
00:09:58.375 --> 00:10:00.206
Is something wrong?

65
00:10:01.111 --> 00:10:04.672
Will you evertell me
about this job?

66
00:10:04.782 --> 00:10:06.215
I promise I will.

67
00:10:08.152 --> 00:10:09.517
See you later.

68
00:10:11.655 --> 00:10:13.350
Before I forget...

69
00:10:13.457 --> 00:10:16.051
Your colleague,
that English guy.

70
00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:17.957
-Jeffrey?
- He called...

71
00:10:18.062 --> 00:10:20.792
Just afteryou left.
Wednesday, I think.

72
00:10:20.898 --> 00:10:25.232
-What did he want?
- I don't know. To speak to you.

73
00:10:25.603 --> 00:10:26.900
See you later.

74
00:10:38.616 --> 00:10:42.279
Listen, Jeffrey.
I told you not to call here.

75
00:10:44.154 --> 00:10:47.715
I already told you.
Muriel is still too weak.

76
00:10:47.825 --> 00:10:50.760
I want to keep her out of all this.

77
00:10:53.063 --> 00:10:55.122
I know I'm not easy to reach.

78
00:10:55.232 --> 00:10:58.326
But I don't want you calling here, OK?

79
00:10:59.737 --> 00:11:04.003
I'm sorry, but I don't have time.
I'll call you later.

80
00:12:23.921 --> 00:12:25.479
Vincent...

81
00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:28.681
Vincent... Wake up.

82
00:12:32.529 --> 00:12:33.621
Hi, Dad.

83
00:12:34.932 --> 00:12:36.456
I didn't hearyou.

84
00:12:38.135 --> 00:12:41.434
What time is it?
I hope the school fair isn't over.

85
00:12:41.538 --> 00:12:44.666
- That's why I'm here.
- Nice of you.

86
00:12:48.812 --> 00:12:49.904
You're so pale.

87
00:12:50.013 --> 00:12:52.573
I don't need a check up.
I'm fine.

88
00:12:52.683 --> 00:12:54.776
But you look tired.

89
00:12:54.885 --> 00:12:57.410
I'm just a little overworked.

90
00:12:57.855 --> 00:13:01.586
So it seems you're applying
for a new job.

91
00:13:01.692 --> 00:13:03.489
News travels fast!

92
00:13:03.827 --> 00:13:05.522
What can you tell us?

93
00:13:05.629 --> 00:13:07.688
My fingers are crossed.

94
00:13:09.466 --> 00:13:13.129
Why hide this from me?
It's silly.

95
00:13:14.438 --> 00:13:17.134
Don't you know how happy I'd be?

96
00:13:23.647 --> 00:13:26.013
How much forthe red one?

97
00:13:26.316 --> 00:13:29.012
- This one?
- No, the other one.

98
00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.512
15 francs.

99
00:13:31.422 --> 00:13:32.650
You're crazy, Felix!

100
00:13:32.756 --> 00:13:35.224
-Why loweryour prices?
- I don't know.

101
00:13:35.492 --> 00:13:37.960
You sold the other one for 30.

102
00:13:38.061 --> 00:13:40.894
I liked the other one.
I don't care about this one.

103
00:13:40.998 --> 00:13:43.990
But he doesn't know that.

104
00:13:46.103 --> 00:13:47.570
I do what I want.

105
00:13:47.671 --> 00:13:49.764
15 francs. It's too late!

106
00:13:51.542 --> 00:13:54.807
Your kid can't appreciate
your commercial strategies.

107
00:13:54.912 --> 00:13:57.745
He's a little reluctant,
but I'll work him over.

108
00:13:58.015 --> 00:14:01.075
Come over here!
Grandpa is buying drinks.

109
00:14:01.185 --> 00:14:02.777
Good news!

110
00:14:02.886 --> 00:14:04.581
Go on. I'll watch the stand.

111
00:14:04.688 --> 00:14:07.384
Keep an eye on Felix.
He's underselling his toys.

112
00:14:07.491 --> 00:14:09.049
Don't worry.

113
00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.958
- Good evening, Luc.
- Good evening, sir.

114
00:14:12.062 --> 00:14:13.859
Have some champagne with us?

115
00:14:13.964 --> 00:14:16.432
Gladly. What's the occasion?

116
00:14:16.533 --> 00:14:20.401
- That's for Vincent to say.
- Stop. I have nothing to tell.

117
00:14:20.504 --> 00:14:25.066
He's changing jobs.
We can't learn more.

118
00:14:25.175 --> 00:14:27.905
- Really, Vincent?
- No... He's dreaming.

119
00:14:28.011 --> 00:14:30.138
I know you.

120
00:14:30.247 --> 00:14:32.044
Nothing's concrete.

121
00:14:32.149 --> 00:14:34.208
- Hello, stranger!
- How are you?

122
00:14:34.318 --> 00:14:35.842
Nice to see you.

123
00:14:36.887 --> 00:14:40.914
-We missed you at Patrick's birthday.
- It's nice to be missed.

124
00:14:41.024 --> 00:14:43.117
- How's the painting?
- Don't ask!

125
00:14:43.227 --> 00:14:45.024
Did you move in?

126
00:14:45.128 --> 00:14:47.596
Two weeks ago.
You stay informed.

127
00:14:47.698 --> 00:14:50.223
We're throwing a housewarming next month.

128
00:14:50.334 --> 00:14:52.894
- Can we count on you?
-Why not...

129
00:14:53.303 --> 00:14:56.101
For now, all of you
come have a drink with us.

130
00:14:56.206 --> 00:14:58.640
Let's celebrate Vincent's new job!

131
00:14:58.742 --> 00:15:00.733
Funny, Muriel never mentioned it.

132
00:15:00.844 --> 00:15:03.779
That's because nothing is sure yet.

133
00:15:04.381 --> 00:15:07.908
- So what's the job?
-We still don't know!

134
00:15:08.018 --> 00:15:10.816
-Will you consult again?
- No thanks!

135
00:15:11.021 --> 00:15:13.717
It has something to do with Switzerland.

136
00:15:13.824 --> 00:15:16.452
The mystery's solved.
He'll work at a bank.

137
00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:17.754
Maybe.

138
00:15:17.861 --> 00:15:20.955
The most important thing
is to be paid in Swiss francs.

139
00:15:21.064 --> 00:15:23.658
- In Geneva?
-You'll all see.

140
00:15:23.767 --> 00:15:27.396
-Are you changing jobs?
- I don't know, honey.

141
00:15:28.972 --> 00:15:30.872
So what can I serve you?

142
00:15:30.974 --> 00:15:33.636
-A cola for me.
- I'll share with her.

143
00:15:33.744 --> 00:15:36.406
You'll have champagne with us!

144
00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.276
That's enough! All those secrets!

145
00:15:39.383 --> 00:15:42.910
Don't get your hopes up.
You'll only be disappointed.

146
00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:44.351
I'm no idiot.

147
00:15:44.454 --> 00:15:47.719
If you weren't sure,
you would have kept silent.

148
00:15:47.824 --> 00:15:49.883
But I didn't say anything!

149
00:15:49.993 --> 00:15:52.461
Do they know at the office?

150
00:15:52.563 --> 00:15:55.430
You can't just drop them like that!

151
00:15:55.899 --> 00:15:58.459
I gave my notice a month ago...

152
00:15:59.202 --> 00:16:02.103
Well, now we can toast in peace!

153
00:16:02.205 --> 00:16:04.537
You have a lot of nerve!

154
00:16:06.276 --> 00:16:08.608
But this is good news, Muriel!

155
00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:12.676
When did you plan on telling me?

156
00:16:13.951 --> 00:16:16.647
This is silly, Muriel. Really!

157
00:16:40.944 --> 00:16:42.502
When do you start?

158
00:16:45.782 --> 00:16:50.219
I go to Switzerland this week
to formalize my contract.

159
00:16:50.621 --> 00:16:52.179
So you start soon?

160
00:16:55.392 --> 00:16:58.088
And you'll be away during the week?

161
00:16:58.195 --> 00:17:01.858
I knew you'd react like this.
That's why I was vague.

162
00:17:02.032 --> 00:17:05.991
How should I react?
We hardly see each other.

163
00:17:06.103 --> 00:17:08.731
I've been fed up with my job
for a while now.

164
00:17:08.839 --> 00:17:12.468
You must have noticed.
I'm really suffocating.

165
00:17:13.443 --> 00:17:15.570
What are you talking about?

166
00:17:15.679 --> 00:17:19.581
I'm not criticizing you
for changing jobs.

167
00:17:37.634 --> 00:17:39.932
So I didn't handle it right.

168
00:17:40.437 --> 00:17:42.803
But this is a chance for me.

169
00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:47.101
It's an interesting job.
You'll be really surprised.

170
00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:50.543
I feel like I've gotten back
some enthusiasm.

171
00:17:50.647 --> 00:17:54.947
All the betterforyou.
It's great to change one's life.

172
00:17:55.619 --> 00:17:59.487
But I'll do like always.
Housework, the kids...

173
00:18:01.291 --> 00:18:04.658
Don't play dumb.
You see the role I'm stuck with.

174
00:18:04.761 --> 00:18:06.922
I never imagined myself like this.

175
00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:10.090
Why not break out of that?

176
00:18:10.534 --> 00:18:14.732
I'll be making a lot of money.
You could do something else.

177
00:18:15.305 --> 00:18:18.604
Go back to school?
Become a professor?

178
00:18:18.709 --> 00:18:21.473
I know you're tired of your job.

179
00:18:21.878 --> 00:18:26.611
You must have other ambitions.
Just teaching...

180
00:18:26.717 --> 00:18:30.016
only 50 meters from home,
always the same faces...

181
00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.554
-What's wrong?
- Nothing.

182
00:18:33.924 --> 00:18:35.357
It's just that...

183
00:18:39.196 --> 00:18:42.597
I never meant to say
that my life was hell.

184
00:18:44.034 --> 00:18:47.868
I'll stop complaining.
I guess I'm just jealous.

185
00:18:58.515 --> 00:19:00.779
Change is important for me.

186
00:19:02.719 --> 00:19:04.414
And not only for me.

187
00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:12.456
You'll see.
Everything will change between us.

188
00:19:12.562 --> 00:19:15.793
-Won't you believe me?
- I don't know.

189
00:19:17.567 --> 00:19:19.660
You've got to trust me.

190
00:19:24.441 --> 00:19:25.669
That little snot!

191
00:19:25.776 --> 00:19:28.301
Acting like he doesn't see us!

192
00:22:33.096 --> 00:22:34.791
- Morning!
- How are you?

193
00:22:34.898 --> 00:22:38.231
- Fine and you?
-Any packages for me?

194
00:22:38.335 --> 00:22:42.328
Nothing yet, but I'll send it over
as soon as it arrives.

195
00:22:42.772 --> 00:22:44.262
Have a good day.

196
00:24:28.144 --> 00:24:29.611
- Hello.
- Hello.

197
00:24:30.780 --> 00:24:35.547
An image problem exists
in the African countries.

198
00:24:36.086 --> 00:24:39.681
The supplied documentation
lists countries

199
00:24:39.789 --> 00:24:45.386
in order of tendency to create
a business-friendly environment.

200
00:24:45.762 --> 00:24:50.062
No surprise to find South Africa
at the top,

201
00:24:50.166 --> 00:24:53.499
followed by Morocco and Egypt.

202
00:24:54.671 --> 00:24:58.539
However, our research revealed
other vital information

203
00:24:59.109 --> 00:25:02.306
on the indicators
of a business-friendly environment.

204
00:25:02.412 --> 00:25:05.108
The most frequently cited
indicators were

205
00:25:05.215 --> 00:25:09.743
healthy government and
strong regulatory setting.

206
00:25:09.853 --> 00:25:15.223
Law enforcement and social stability
rank third.

207
00:25:51.261 --> 00:25:54.162
Only administrative details
to work out now.

208
00:25:54.264 --> 00:25:58.633
I'll visit the offices,
get to know the departments...

209
00:26:00.370 --> 00:26:03.771
Yeah, things are moving fast.
The least one could say!

210
00:26:03.873 --> 00:26:06.137
I could be starting on Monday!

211
00:26:06.509 --> 00:26:09.672
-We'll talk this weekend, OK?
- Sir...

212
00:26:10.213 --> 00:26:11.703
I've got to go...

213
00:26:12.515 --> 00:26:13.641
Kisses, bye.

214
00:26:14.751 --> 00:26:16.651
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

215
00:26:16.753 --> 00:26:19.051
- Do you work here, sir?
- No.

216
00:26:19.155 --> 00:26:21.749
Maybe you have an appointment?

217
00:26:21.858 --> 00:26:24.759
Not really. ljust left one.

218
00:26:24.861 --> 00:26:26.658
You had an appointment with?

219
00:26:26.763 --> 00:26:29.698
Maybe I don't have the right
to stay here?

220
00:26:29.799 --> 00:26:30.823
It's just that...

221
00:26:30.934 --> 00:26:33.129
You've been here for an hour, sir.

222
00:26:33.236 --> 00:26:35.295
I'll be on my way.

223
00:26:35.405 --> 00:26:37.839
- I don't mean to chase you off.
- No problem.

224
00:26:37.941 --> 00:26:40.637
Weren't you given a pass at reception?

225
00:26:40.743 --> 00:26:42.904
Don't worry about it.

226
00:26:43.379 --> 00:26:47.577
I'm sorry.
This isn't a public space.

227
00:28:09.832 --> 00:28:14.826
"Note on the dynamic evolution
between UCDI and NGOs."

228
00:28:15.338 --> 00:28:19.502
"Note on the dynamic evolution
between UCDI and NGOs.

229
00:28:19.609 --> 00:28:23.636
"A certain number of internal
agency procedures were revised

230
00:28:23.746 --> 00:28:27.147
"in orderto encourage
involvement of NGOs

231
00:28:27.250 --> 00:28:30.048
"in UCDI programs and projects.

232
00:28:32.021 --> 00:28:34.819
"The Secretary General of UCDl,

233
00:28:35.558 --> 00:28:39.085
"Mr. Walter Ribeiro,
recalled in the last forum

234
00:28:39.195 --> 00:28:44.462
"that the agency-NGO collaboration
made more than 800 projects happen

235
00:28:44.567 --> 00:28:49.527
"in direct coordination
with local chambers of commerce."

236
00:29:28.678 --> 00:29:29.770
Go, Julien!

237
00:30:02.645 --> 00:30:06.513
Felix, we'll wait for him here.
He's still busy.

238
00:30:12.588 --> 00:30:14.180
Good job, mister!

239
00:30:14.557 --> 00:30:17.651
I thought he'd take you down.
He was 10 cm taller.

240
00:30:17.760 --> 00:30:19.591
But he's a big softy.

241
00:30:22.632 --> 00:30:23.758
Let's fight!

242
00:30:25.868 --> 00:30:28.166
-You're in a hurry?
- Can't miss the bus.

243
00:30:28.271 --> 00:30:31.206
- Not coming with us?
- I made other plans.

244
00:30:31.307 --> 00:30:34.504
-We drove 200 kilometres.
- Hey, I didn't ask you to!

245
00:30:34.610 --> 00:30:38.478
I know I spend more time in Switzerland
than with you.

246
00:30:38.581 --> 00:30:42.483
- It's not easy for any of us.
- No problem, Dad!

247
00:30:53.296 --> 00:30:56.493
- How did you do that?
- Happened in the match.

248
00:30:56.599 --> 00:30:57.725
When he grabbed you.

249
00:30:57.834 --> 00:31:01.531
-Are you happy?
-Yeah, I felt good out there.

250
00:31:01.637 --> 00:31:04.470
What a show-off!
But you were good.

251
00:31:04.574 --> 00:31:07.441
It was super. Now run along.

252
00:31:09.545 --> 00:31:11.536
We're eating at your grandparents.

253
00:31:11.647 --> 00:31:14.081
You can't believe he'll come!

254
00:31:15.485 --> 00:31:18.318
Felix, come back here!

255
00:31:25.895 --> 00:31:28.455
Are you sure there isn't another way?

256
00:31:28.564 --> 00:31:29.861
What other way?

257
00:31:30.199 --> 00:31:32.394
Maybe...

258
00:31:32.502 --> 00:31:35.767
If you insist, you could get housing.

259
00:31:35.872 --> 00:31:39.968
Surely the UN has housing
to offerto its executives.

260
00:31:40.076 --> 00:31:43.807
Maybe for other departments,
but not in my case.

261
00:31:43.913 --> 00:31:47.405
All my colleagues
are in the same situation.

262
00:31:54.824 --> 00:31:56.519
You're sure this isn't a mistake?

263
00:31:56.626 --> 00:31:59.789
How irritating!
It's as if I'm forcing you.

264
00:31:59.896 --> 00:32:01.796
- Take it easy.
- Listen, Dad...

265
00:32:01.898 --> 00:32:04.492
I only need 200,000 francs
to get set up.

266
00:32:04.600 --> 00:32:07.501
If you don't want to,
I'll find another way.

267
00:32:07.603 --> 00:32:10.003
Don't use that tone with me.

268
00:32:11.941 --> 00:32:14.375
Couldn't you rent something?

269
00:32:15.511 --> 00:32:18.605
It's just going to increase
your household bills.

270
00:32:18.714 --> 00:32:19.806
Exactly.

271
00:32:20.383 --> 00:32:22.851
That's why we called on you.

272
00:32:23.219 --> 00:32:25.414
We did our calculations.

273
00:32:25.521 --> 00:32:30.481
Vincent's housing stipends
will help reimburse you overtwo years.

274
00:32:30.960 --> 00:32:33.952
We'd be saving money
if he didn't stay in a hotel.

275
00:32:34.063 --> 00:32:38.227
You've made your point!
You've done your research.

276
00:32:45.241 --> 00:32:47.766
200,000?

277
00:32:47.877 --> 00:32:49.242
That will do it.

278
00:32:50.947 --> 00:32:52.574
What are you doing?

279
00:32:52.815 --> 00:32:55.181
Giving money to yourfather.

280
00:32:56.085 --> 00:32:57.916
Will you give me some, too?

281
00:32:58.020 --> 00:32:59.817
- Felix, really!
-You little fox!

282
00:32:59.922 --> 00:33:03.915
By giving to yourfather,
I'm also giving to you.

283
00:33:04.193 --> 00:33:05.285
Thanks, Dad.

284
00:33:05.761 --> 00:33:07.490
And that's foryou.

285
00:33:07.597 --> 00:33:10.327
But I expect a kiss of thanks.

286
00:33:22.178 --> 00:33:24.078
Look, Mom! See what I made?

287
00:33:24.180 --> 00:33:26.273
That's nice. Let's go.

288
00:33:27.450 --> 00:33:29.941
So soon? We've hardly spoken!

289
00:33:30.052 --> 00:33:33.544
I'm sorry,
but the kids are really tired.

290
00:33:33.656 --> 00:33:36.318
You didn't tell me
how your job is going.

291
00:33:36.425 --> 00:33:39.019
Great. Shoes on, Felix.

292
00:33:39.228 --> 00:33:42.857
I had dinner with Fremont recently.

293
00:33:43.466 --> 00:33:47.129
His face, when I told him
you worked forthe UN...

294
00:33:47.236 --> 00:33:49.898
I can count on you
to tell the whole world!

295
00:33:50.006 --> 00:33:51.132
Hold on...

296
00:33:51.240 --> 00:33:55.506
International posts are privileged. Something to be proud of.

297
00:33:55.611 --> 00:33:57.943
That's true. We're like princes.

298
00:33:59.048 --> 00:34:02.506
There are times...
It's almost shocking.

299
00:34:02.852 --> 00:34:07.016
The other day,
I was phoning a guy from Mozambique.

300
00:34:07.123 --> 00:34:11.890
He's fighting to reconstruct
theirtelecommunications network.

301
00:34:11.994 --> 00:34:14.690
Suddenly I looked around me...

302
00:34:16.032 --> 00:34:19.490
All the marble and glass...

303
00:34:20.770 --> 00:34:21.794
All the space...

304
00:34:21.904 --> 00:34:23.667
And you're complaining?

305
00:34:23.773 --> 00:34:26.503
No, it's just surrealistic.

306
00:34:26.609 --> 00:34:27.974
Let's go, Alice.

307
00:34:46.262 --> 00:34:50.198
It's a nice surprise
to see you so enthusiastic.

308
00:34:52.034 --> 00:34:53.433
Good night, Dad.

309
00:35:20.429 --> 00:35:24.525
"Natural resources are the main interest
of foreign investors,

310
00:35:24.967 --> 00:35:29.597
"although there is an influx
toward industry and service.

311
00:35:30.272 --> 00:35:34.868
"Privatization results in attracting
direct foreign investment to Africa,

312
00:35:34.977 --> 00:35:38.469
"more so during the '90s
than in previous decades.

313
00:35:39.348 --> 00:35:42.078
"Between 1990 and 1998,

314
00:35:42.551 --> 00:35:47.284
"there was a great deal of privatization
in South Africa,

315
00:35:47.823 --> 00:35:50.053
"$1.4 billion,

316
00:35:50.526 --> 00:35:53.256
"Ghana, $769 million,

317
00:35:53.763 --> 00:35:56.254
"Nigeria, $500 million,

318
00:35:57.099 --> 00:35:59.158
"Zambia, $420 million,

319
00:35:59.268 --> 00:36:02.135
"and Ivory Coast, $373 million."

320
00:36:51.053 --> 00:36:54.887
They took my truck.
They brought me to a place.

321
00:36:54.990 --> 00:36:57.288
I spent half an hourthere.

322
00:36:57.393 --> 00:37:00.521
I was really scared.
I prayed in the sleeper.

323
00:37:00.629 --> 00:37:02.324
Holding the pistol like this...

324
00:37:02.431 --> 00:37:05.764
They took all my money
and credit cards.

325
00:37:05.868 --> 00:37:10.066
They took me back.
They took my jacket and...

326
00:37:11.073 --> 00:37:14.372
- They left you like that?
- In my underwear!

327
00:37:26.155 --> 00:37:28.214
Fred, I'm suspicious...

328
00:37:28.324 --> 00:37:31.259
I see canned ravioli
when I think of you.

329
00:37:31.360 --> 00:37:34.056
You still have that butane burner?

330
00:37:37.733 --> 00:37:41.931
No, I don't trust you.
I'd rather go to a restaurant.

331
00:37:45.140 --> 00:37:48.109
Yeah, my job is going well.

332
00:37:48.577 --> 00:37:52.946
I'll tell you all about it.
I've got a proposal foryou.

333
00:37:54.583 --> 00:37:57.416
I'd rathertalk about it later.

334
00:37:58.120 --> 00:38:01.920
I arrive in Grenoble around 6:00.
That OK foryou?

335
00:38:04.493 --> 00:38:06.654
OK, Fred...

336
00:38:07.196 --> 00:38:09.255
See you at the Novotel.

337
00:38:09.431 --> 00:38:11.160
See you later.

338
00:39:02.818 --> 00:39:06.413
- Fred, you can't dump us!
- I'll be right back.

339
00:39:11.427 --> 00:39:14.225
- I'm really happy to see you.
- Me, too.

340
00:39:14.930 --> 00:39:17.956
ljust need a couple minutes
for a group photo.

341
00:39:18.067 --> 00:39:19.898
Go on. I understand.

342
00:39:20.436 --> 00:39:23.098
Mr Pradal, this is Vincent Renault.

343
00:39:23.205 --> 00:39:24.968
- Hello, Vincent.
- Hello, sir.

344
00:39:25.074 --> 00:39:27.167
Vincent worked foryears
at DR Consulting.

345
00:39:27.276 --> 00:39:28.368
Very good.

346
00:39:28.577 --> 00:39:31.444
He's left the area.
We lost contact for a while.

347
00:39:31.547 --> 00:39:34.141
- The big reunion!
- Sort of.

348
00:39:34.917 --> 00:39:35.906
So, where to?

349
00:39:36.018 --> 00:39:38.418
You can all go to the patio.

350
00:39:38.821 --> 00:39:40.584
I'll have them light it.

351
00:39:40.689 --> 00:39:41.849
Excuse me.

352
00:39:42.691 --> 00:39:45.592
-Are you coming?
- No, it's cold.

353
00:40:19.395 --> 00:40:22.626
ljust took a chance
and it worked out.

354
00:40:22.731 --> 00:40:24.460
It's all up to you.

355
00:40:24.867 --> 00:40:28.132
There are so many businesses
gravitating around the UN.

356
00:40:28.237 --> 00:40:30.364
They always need new collaborators.

357
00:40:30.472 --> 00:40:32.702
As if they're waiting on me!

358
00:40:32.808 --> 00:40:36.039
I don't have the right profile.
No international experience.

359
00:40:36.145 --> 00:40:39.444
Think again!
What's needed are collaborators.

360
00:40:39.548 --> 00:40:42.847
Consultants with experience
in the private sector.

361
00:40:42.951 --> 00:40:46.785
If ever I need to expand my team,
I'd surely think of you.

362
00:40:46.889 --> 00:40:49.722
I'm just a complainer.
I don't care about work.

363
00:40:49.825 --> 00:40:51.554
I'm not ambitious.

364
00:40:52.027 --> 00:40:55.121
I could never be passionate
about a job.

365
00:40:55.230 --> 00:40:58.859
-And your work friends?
-You saved me!

366
00:40:59.334 --> 00:41:02.929
Dinner with the boss?
Give me a break!

367
00:41:03.038 --> 00:41:05.233
I need my space.

368
00:41:05.340 --> 00:41:06.967
It's not easy.

369
00:41:07.076 --> 00:41:09.977
But doing less gets boring.

370
00:41:10.779 --> 00:41:14.271
Sometimes after work,
ljust can't go home.

371
00:41:14.516 --> 00:41:16.916
I have to see people.

372
00:41:17.019 --> 00:41:20.750
Go out, feel like
I did something with my day.

373
00:41:21.457 --> 00:41:23.857
Give myself
some kind of stupid pleasure.

374
00:41:23.959 --> 00:41:27.554
I tend to forget
that all that costs money.

375
00:41:29.198 --> 00:41:31.428
That's why your investment offer...

376
00:41:32.167 --> 00:41:33.998
Well, I'm interested.

377
00:41:34.770 --> 00:41:36.738
But I don't have
a whole lot put aside.

378
00:41:36.839 --> 00:41:40.240
50,000 francs in savings...

379
00:41:41.577 --> 00:41:43.408
Don't know if it's worth it.

380
00:41:43.512 --> 00:41:45.742
I swear it's worth it!

381
00:41:45.848 --> 00:41:48.646
I don't know, either
what it means to economize.

382
00:41:48.750 --> 00:41:52.186
That's exactly why
this is a good solution.

383
00:41:52.287 --> 00:41:55.347
I guess I didn't look at it
that way.

384
00:41:56.258 --> 00:42:00.388
This investment is just an example.

385
00:42:00.662 --> 00:42:03.460
Trust me,
I don't go into things blindly.

386
00:42:03.565 --> 00:42:06.033
The colleague who let me in on it...

387
00:42:06.135 --> 00:42:07.966
He only works with Eastern Europe.

388
00:42:08.070 --> 00:42:12.097
He's an expert.
He'll run the whole thing.

389
00:42:12.574 --> 00:42:14.508
The money he made in two years!

390
00:42:14.610 --> 00:42:15.804
Unbelievable!

391
00:42:16.278 --> 00:42:18.371
Isn't it a big risk foryou?

392
00:42:18.914 --> 00:42:22.680
Currency can't be carried
in the diplomatic pouch.

393
00:42:22.784 --> 00:42:25.947
But there are no controls.
So no real danger.

394
00:42:29.224 --> 00:42:32.057
I'll have the money
tomorrow morning.

395
00:42:32.161 --> 00:42:34.857
No good for me.
I'm leaving for Geneva.

396
00:42:36.165 --> 00:42:40.397
Here's what we'll do...
We'll hook up next week.

397
00:42:40.936 --> 00:42:41.994
Sounds good.

398
00:42:42.404 --> 00:42:45.373
- Monday?
- Perfect.

399
00:42:47.209 --> 00:42:49.143
-At 9:00?
- 9:00 it is.

400
00:42:53.382 --> 00:42:54.440
Bye, Fred.

401
00:42:54.750 --> 00:42:56.183
See you Monday.

402
00:42:56.552 --> 00:42:58.019
Have a safe trip.

403
00:43:44.967 --> 00:43:46.229
Mister!

404
00:43:47.869 --> 00:43:50.201
Please loweryour window.

405
00:43:54.443 --> 00:43:55.967
Good evening, sir.

406
00:43:56.712 --> 00:43:59.613
This is a private lot.
Did you know that?

407
00:44:00.849 --> 00:44:02.339
This is a hotel, sir.

408
00:44:02.451 --> 00:44:05.147
Lots of rooms to sleep in.
You can't stay on the lot.

409
00:44:05.254 --> 00:44:06.278
Very funny!

410
00:44:06.622 --> 00:44:09.887
Sir, I tried to be polite.
Now get the hell out of here!

411
00:44:09.992 --> 00:44:12.051
Humor goes away quickly!

412
00:44:12.160 --> 00:44:13.388
Get a move on!

413
00:44:13.795 --> 00:44:15.695
Go on! Get out!

414
00:44:15.797 --> 00:44:17.731
All right, all right...

415
00:44:44.826 --> 00:44:45.986
Sure you won't come along, Julien?

416
00:44:47.562 --> 00:44:48.961
Is there a code?

417
00:44:51.633 --> 00:44:54.227
Hang up, Julien.
I'm speaking to you!

418
00:44:54.703 --> 00:44:56.762
I have to go. Bye.

419
00:44:57.973 --> 00:45:00.908
We gave you that phone
so your mother could reach you.

420
00:45:01.009 --> 00:45:02.704
Not to spend hours with friends.

421
00:45:02.811 --> 00:45:06.144
I don't want to go shopping.
I have other plans.

422
00:45:06.348 --> 00:45:07.474
Really?

423
00:45:07.849 --> 00:45:09.749
And what are those plans?

424
00:45:09.851 --> 00:45:11.409
Nothing special.

425
00:45:11.853 --> 00:45:13.718
Call some friends...

426
00:45:14.056 --> 00:45:16.718
Maybe go to the movies.

427
00:45:18.460 --> 00:45:19.927
Just hanging out!

428
00:45:25.067 --> 00:45:26.364
Here, Julien...

429
00:45:30.505 --> 00:45:32.166
What are you doing, Vincent?

430
00:45:32.741 --> 00:45:35.107
This is between Julien and I.

431
00:45:35.210 --> 00:45:39.374
500 francs to a kid!
That's a lot of money.

432
00:45:39.548 --> 00:45:43.211
He's old enough to buy clothes
on his own.

433
00:45:43.318 --> 00:45:46.151
You're dreaming to think
he'll buy clothes!

434
00:45:46.254 --> 00:45:48.779
I always choose them anyway.

435
00:45:49.891 --> 00:45:53.452
Don't get used to it.
This is an exceptional gift.

436
00:45:58.734 --> 00:46:00.361
I don't like red!

437
00:46:00.469 --> 00:46:04.200
Try on the red.
We'll find another color, OK?

438
00:46:04.740 --> 00:46:07.709
It looks nice on you.

439
00:46:09.177 --> 00:46:11.236
- Does it feel good?
-Yeah.

440
00:46:12.047 --> 00:46:13.173
No.

441
00:46:14.616 --> 00:46:16.345
You'll never wear it.

442
00:46:16.451 --> 00:46:18.180
That's the one I like!

443
00:46:18.286 --> 00:46:22.120
I'd preferto buy you
something you'd wear often.

444
00:46:22.224 --> 00:46:25.022
Mom, just let me
buy herthe pants.

445
00:46:25.127 --> 00:46:27.027
Find something else
you want to buy for her.

446
00:46:27.129 --> 00:46:29.563
I don't mind buying the pants.

447
00:46:29.664 --> 00:46:32.963
Isn't that Jeffrey overthere?

448
00:46:33.969 --> 00:46:35.266
Yes, it's him.

449
00:46:48.583 --> 00:46:50.847
-Vincent. How are you?
-Well, and you?

450
00:46:50.952 --> 00:46:52.214
I'm fine.

451
00:46:52.454 --> 00:46:54.081
My wife, Elizabeth.

452
00:46:55.390 --> 00:46:56.789
Our little Lola.

453
00:46:58.326 --> 00:46:59.691
My wife, Muriel.

454
00:47:01.029 --> 00:47:03.623
-We've met before...
-Afew years ago.

455
00:47:03.732 --> 00:47:06.633
I told Vincent
you looked familiar.

456
00:47:07.502 --> 00:47:09.333
- Sure you're all right?
- Fine.

457
00:47:09.438 --> 00:47:12.805
- Should we have a smoke?
- If you'd like.

458
00:47:32.427 --> 00:47:37.228
I didn't want to harass you.
My calls were only to help you.

459
00:47:37.332 --> 00:47:38.356
Help me?

460
00:47:38.633 --> 00:47:41.500
Did you listen to my messages?

461
00:47:41.603 --> 00:47:43.002
Of course, I heard them.

462
00:47:43.104 --> 00:47:46.870
I contacted other companies
ready to hire you.

463
00:47:46.975 --> 00:47:48.203
It's OK.

464
00:47:48.777 --> 00:47:49.903
How OK?

465
00:47:50.011 --> 00:47:51.979
I'm fine. Why do you insist?

466
00:47:52.080 --> 00:47:54.378
Vincent, you were fired.

467
00:47:54.483 --> 00:47:57.850
Then you completely disappear.
My concern is normal.

468
00:47:57.953 --> 00:48:00.820
I don't find it normal.
We only worked together.

469
00:48:00.922 --> 00:48:02.287
Is this a joke?

470
00:48:02.624 --> 00:48:04.854
Weren't we really close?

471
00:48:04.960 --> 00:48:07.861
We ate lunch together
daily for 10 years.

472
00:48:07.963 --> 00:48:11.399
All those late evenings...
Isn't that something?

473
00:48:11.500 --> 00:48:14.298
That means nothing now.
I have a new job.

474
00:48:14.402 --> 00:48:17.166
-What?
- It's going really well.

475
00:48:18.039 --> 00:48:19.973
Why didn't you tell me?

476
00:48:20.308 --> 00:48:22.299
You're really strange.

477
00:48:25.080 --> 00:48:27.514
-And your wife?
- Leave her alone.

478
00:48:27.616 --> 00:48:29.447
You said she was doing badly.

479
00:48:29.551 --> 00:48:33.317
What a miracle!
She's cured of her depression?

480
00:48:33.421 --> 00:48:36.288
She doesn't know
that I've been let go.

481
00:48:36.391 --> 00:48:39.292
-What?
- She thinks I resigned.

482
00:48:39.394 --> 00:48:40.622
You're crazy!

483
00:48:41.463 --> 00:48:42.760
That's stupid.

484
00:48:43.465 --> 00:48:45.524
Your opinion doesn't interest me.

485
00:48:45.634 --> 00:48:47.499
I'm fine. What else matters?

486
00:48:48.803 --> 00:48:51.465
Leave me alone. Is that clear?

487
00:48:53.875 --> 00:48:55.399
Just like twins!

488
00:49:24.306 --> 00:49:26.206
How are you, Vincent?

489
00:49:26.308 --> 00:49:27.900
-And you?
- Real good.

490
00:49:28.009 --> 00:49:29.567
This is Philippe.

491
00:49:30.645 --> 00:49:31.737
Have a seat.

492
00:49:38.320 --> 00:49:39.548
Do you remember Philippe?

493
00:49:42.490 --> 00:49:44.720
I'm not sure...

494
00:49:44.826 --> 00:49:47.021
He was one year after us.

495
00:49:47.128 --> 00:49:49.187
No, I don't remember. Sorry.

496
00:49:49.297 --> 00:49:51.697
- It might come to me.
- I hope so.

497
00:49:51.800 --> 00:49:54.598
I filled him in.
Hope it's no problem.

498
00:49:54.703 --> 00:49:57.797
No, but my first priority
has been to contact

499
00:49:57.906 --> 00:49:59.669
people that I know.

500
00:49:59.774 --> 00:50:01.435
Easierto keep track of.

501
00:50:01.543 --> 00:50:03.443
Philippe is interested.

502
00:50:04.145 --> 00:50:05.305
Very much so.

503
00:50:06.314 --> 00:50:10.216
He's a better client.
He's got more money.

504
00:50:10.318 --> 00:50:11.580
More money!

505
00:50:12.821 --> 00:50:16.018
- Probably about 300,000 francs.
- See what I mean?

506
00:50:16.958 --> 00:50:19.119
That's no problem at all!

507
00:50:20.028 --> 00:50:22.087
Did Fred explain what to expect?

508
00:50:22.197 --> 00:50:25.860
He spelled out the basic terms.
Can I know more?

509
00:50:25.967 --> 00:50:27.127
Of course!

510
00:50:27.902 --> 00:50:32.066
Concretely, we give money.
Then an account is opened.

511
00:50:32.607 --> 00:50:34.632
The money works... And then?

512
00:50:35.143 --> 00:50:38.237
How do we keep track?
Do you send bank statements?

513
00:50:38.346 --> 00:50:42.112
I made that clearto Fred.
You receive nothing.

514
00:50:42.217 --> 00:50:44.651
- It's real clearto me.
- Not for me!

515
00:50:44.753 --> 00:50:48.018
Listen... Let me make this clear.

516
00:50:48.723 --> 00:50:51.214
The accounts are numbered.

517
00:50:51.960 --> 00:50:53.120
They're unofficial.

518
00:50:53.228 --> 00:50:55.594
- Not really legal.
- I got that.

519
00:50:55.697 --> 00:50:57.528
For now, of course...

520
00:50:57.932 --> 00:51:00.924
I'll stay in touch,
keep you posted.

521
00:51:01.169 --> 00:51:03.000
Keep a close eye on things.

522
00:51:03.104 --> 00:51:05.572
I told him how much
you'll make off of us.

523
00:51:05.674 --> 00:51:08.507
Great that he'll make money
off of us.

524
00:51:08.610 --> 00:51:10.601
But I need more than that.

525
00:51:11.012 --> 00:51:13.412
I'm interested, but I need more.

526
00:51:13.515 --> 00:51:15.506
To invest 300,000 francs...

527
00:51:15.617 --> 00:51:18.609
I need some kind of paper.

528
00:51:18.720 --> 00:51:20.711
A receipt, or something!

529
00:51:20.822 --> 00:51:22.653
I'm not joking!

530
00:51:22.757 --> 00:51:24.247
For 300,000 francs!

531
00:51:24.359 --> 00:51:26.520
Listen, Fred, this is normal.

532
00:51:26.628 --> 00:51:28.391
I'll sign something foryou, too.

533
00:51:28.496 --> 00:51:32.455
- It's OK. I really don't need it.
-Well, I do!

534
00:51:46.381 --> 00:51:47.973
These...

535
00:51:48.950 --> 00:51:51.578
are the forms to open an account.

536
00:51:52.253 --> 00:51:53.982
Read them carefully.

537
00:51:54.089 --> 00:51:56.182
Think it over, Philippe.

538
00:51:57.726 --> 00:52:00.217
Don't want you
coming into this backwards.

539
00:52:00.729 --> 00:52:02.219
I need some time.

540
00:52:03.198 --> 00:52:05.792
I'm interested,
but I'd like to look this over

541
00:52:05.900 --> 00:52:08.164
calmly, with a clear head.

542
00:52:08.603 --> 00:52:11.902
I suggest meeting again.

543
00:52:12.006 --> 00:52:14.031
But I am interested.

544
00:52:44.639 --> 00:52:46.334
- Hello.
- Hello.

545
00:52:46.775 --> 00:52:49.869
I'd like to speak to you
if you're free.

546
00:52:49.978 --> 00:52:51.138
About what?

547
00:52:51.679 --> 00:52:53.670
About Switzerland, for example.

548
00:52:53.782 --> 00:52:55.545
- Switzerland?
-Yes.

549
00:52:58.887 --> 00:53:01.253
I don't really have the time today.

550
00:53:01.356 --> 00:53:04.951
I'm working all week.
It will be difficult.

551
00:53:05.527 --> 00:53:08.155
I've got all the time in the world.

552
00:53:09.597 --> 00:53:11.792
Call me wheneveryou want.

553
00:53:12.233 --> 00:53:14.292
- See you soon.
- Thanks.

554
00:53:30.718 --> 00:53:34.381
"The UCDI and France have signed
an investment agreement

555
00:53:34.489 --> 00:53:39.188
"for a project to reinforce
training in international commerce

556
00:53:39.294 --> 00:53:43.128
"for Benin, Mali and Burkina-Faso.

557
00:53:43.231 --> 00:53:46.564
"The amount is 2,284,000 francs.

558
00:53:47.936 --> 00:53:50.063
"The agreement foresees:

559
00:53:50.705 --> 00:53:53.936
"creating specialized training centers,

560
00:53:54.409 --> 00:53:57.207
"organizing seminars,
both national and regional,

561
00:53:57.312 --> 00:54:00.145
"on international commerce issues,

562
00:54:00.782 --> 00:54:04.240
"conceiving, adapting and updating

563
00:54:05.053 --> 00:54:09.012
"multidisciplinary teaching units
that respond to the needs

564
00:54:09.123 --> 00:54:12.923
"of executives
in public and private sectors."

565
00:55:29.971 --> 00:55:31.097
Enjoy it!

566
00:56:18.786 --> 00:56:21.880
- Does Mom know?
- No, I want to surprise her.

567
00:56:21.990 --> 00:56:23.287
How much did it cost?

568
00:56:23.691 --> 00:56:25.022
145,000 francs.

569
00:56:25.126 --> 00:56:28.459
- It was on sale?
- But it's almost new.

570
00:56:28.563 --> 00:56:32.226
Jerome's dad paid 330,000.

571
00:56:32.600 --> 00:56:35.034
Well, I'm not Jerome's dad.

572
00:56:36.337 --> 00:56:39.670
Sorry, Julien,
I've got another call.

573
00:56:39.774 --> 00:56:41.036
Call you tomorrow.

574
00:56:41.142 --> 00:56:43.508
- OK, Dad. Bye.
- Bye. Kisses.

575
00:56:50.518 --> 00:56:51.917
Who's speaking?

576
00:56:52.420 --> 00:56:54.251
Don't you know me?

577
00:56:57.792 --> 00:56:59.350
Try harder!

578
00:57:04.232 --> 00:57:05.460
Is that Nono?

579
00:57:06.701 --> 00:57:07.827
You got it!

580
00:57:12.473 --> 00:57:13.963
Nothing to say?

581
00:57:16.944 --> 00:57:18.138
Where are you?

582
00:57:18.946 --> 00:57:21.972
What do you mean?
Did I wake you?

583
00:57:22.083 --> 00:57:24.950
I'm just surprised, that's all.

584
00:57:25.053 --> 00:57:28.580
Fred told me
you've been around Grenoble.

585
00:57:28.689 --> 00:57:30.350
You could have called.

586
00:57:30.458 --> 00:57:33.859
Fred didn't tell me
you two were in touch.

587
00:57:34.962 --> 00:57:37.260
So when can you come by?

588
00:57:37.465 --> 00:57:40.832
I don't think I can.
I'm sorry.

589
00:57:41.402 --> 00:57:42.960
That's too bad.

590
00:57:43.071 --> 00:57:46.632
It's possible on Friday.
Around 6:00 p.m.

591
00:57:46.741 --> 00:57:50.142
We'll expect you for dinner.
Friday's perfect.

592
00:58:00.421 --> 00:58:03.720
- Still recognize me?
- Of course I do.

593
00:58:10.665 --> 00:58:11.757
He's here!

594
00:58:13.568 --> 00:58:15.001
-Jeanne.
-Vincent.

595
00:58:15.103 --> 00:58:17.230
- Nice to meet you.
- It's my pleasure.

596
00:58:17.338 --> 00:58:18.771
You shouldn't have.

597
00:58:18.873 --> 00:58:21.171
It's OK. He's not hurting.

598
00:58:22.176 --> 00:58:23.905
- That's Julie.
- Hi, Julie.

599
00:58:24.011 --> 00:58:26.445
Say hello to Vincent, Julie.

600
00:58:26.981 --> 00:58:28.471
He won't bite you!

601
00:58:28.583 --> 00:58:30.551
What's wrong?
Usually not so shy.

602
00:58:30.651 --> 00:58:32.141
That suit scares her!

603
00:58:32.253 --> 00:58:34.050
Don't make fun of me!

604
00:58:34.789 --> 00:58:38.088
- Come on in...
- Let me take your coat.

605
00:58:38.593 --> 00:58:41.153
I'll put the flowers in a vase.

606
00:58:41.462 --> 00:58:44.625
Let me show you the apartment.

607
00:58:46.834 --> 00:58:48.062
This here...

608
00:58:48.469 --> 00:58:50.096
This is my refuge.

609
00:58:51.906 --> 00:58:54.704
You've got a lot of equipment.

610
00:58:55.176 --> 00:58:58.077
You've made a real sound studio.

611
00:58:59.113 --> 00:59:02.048
It's not professional equipment,
but it's a start.

612
00:59:02.150 --> 00:59:04.914
- Do you give concerts?
- No.

613
00:59:05.286 --> 00:59:08.983
Just play for myself
or with friends.

614
00:59:09.090 --> 00:59:12.890
- Let's hear something.
- I'm not ready yet.

615
00:59:12.994 --> 00:59:14.791
I'd really like to hear.

616
00:59:14.896 --> 00:59:17.729
But I'm still a little nervous.

617
00:59:17.832 --> 00:59:20.062
Betterto listen when it's ready.

618
00:59:20.168 --> 00:59:22.159
So what else are you up to?

619
00:59:22.270 --> 00:59:23.897
Working?

620
00:59:24.539 --> 00:59:25.597
A lot.

621
00:59:27.041 --> 00:59:29.407
- I'm always working.
- I see...

622
00:59:29.510 --> 00:59:31.273
You're a kept man!

623
00:59:31.379 --> 00:59:34.075
Not at all. I'm happy to work.

624
00:59:34.415 --> 00:59:38.283
He concentrates on his music
and takes care of the kid.

625
00:59:38.386 --> 00:59:41.150
He'll soon be calling me a pimp!

626
00:59:41.856 --> 00:59:43.414
Really, it's clear...

627
00:59:43.524 --> 00:59:47.051
Geneva isn't a very lively city.

628
00:59:47.328 --> 00:59:49.455
It's very cosmopolitan.

629
00:59:49.564 --> 00:59:51.759
But I'm always seeing
the same faces.

630
00:59:51.866 --> 00:59:55.495
Either major corporate guys
or bankers.

631
00:59:56.671 --> 00:59:58.434
Movers and shakers like you.

632
00:59:59.407 --> 01:00:01.238
Stop kidding around.

633
01:00:01.742 --> 01:00:04.404
I don't shake up a whole lot.

634
01:00:04.512 --> 01:00:06.776
But your job seems so interesting.

635
01:00:06.881 --> 01:00:10.681
It must be so gratifying
to be helping out Africa.

636
01:00:10.785 --> 01:00:13.379
Betterthan working
for some private company.

637
01:00:13.487 --> 01:00:15.216
Yes, I'm very happy.

638
01:00:15.323 --> 01:00:19.054
But I've only had the post
for a month and a half.

639
01:00:19.160 --> 01:00:21.355
I don't feel
as if I've helped yet.

640
01:00:21.796 --> 01:00:23.559
Don't be so modest.

641
01:00:23.664 --> 01:00:26.132
- It's great what you do.
-You're making fun again.

642
01:00:26.234 --> 01:00:27.258
Not at all.

643
01:00:27.368 --> 01:00:28.892
I'm truly happy foryou!

644
01:00:29.003 --> 01:00:31.437
I think it's true.
He admires you a lot!

645
01:00:31.539 --> 01:00:34.508
Don't go too far.
It'll go to his head.

646
01:00:34.609 --> 01:00:36.236
You call that admiration?

647
01:00:37.345 --> 01:00:41.611
No declarations of love!
You're invited for other reasons.

648
01:00:41.716 --> 01:00:43.343
I feel much better.

649
01:00:43.451 --> 01:00:45.851
Don't you know what I mean?

650
01:00:46.520 --> 01:00:49.216
Fred told me
about the Swiss venture.

651
01:00:50.057 --> 01:00:51.081
Really?

652
01:00:52.627 --> 01:00:55.391
I neverthought you'd be interested.

653
01:00:55.496 --> 01:00:56.690
Why shouldn't I be?

654
01:00:56.797 --> 01:01:00.927
You told Fred, Serge
and who knows how many others.

655
01:01:01.969 --> 01:01:03.300
Can't I want money?

656
01:01:03.871 --> 01:01:07.637
Sorry, ljust neverthought...

657
01:01:07.975 --> 01:01:11.877
We're actually very interested.
We put a little money aside.

658
01:01:12.013 --> 01:01:14.481
Only 12,000 francs, but...

659
01:01:14.582 --> 01:01:15.810
Stop right there!

660
01:01:15.916 --> 01:01:18.544
I don't want to.
Not with you two!

661
01:01:18.653 --> 01:01:20.883
Why not? We want to.

662
01:01:20.988 --> 01:01:23.456
What is it?
12,000 isn't enough?

663
01:01:23.557 --> 01:01:24.649
It's not that.

664
01:01:24.759 --> 01:01:27.990
But small sums
don't make a whole lot.

665
01:01:28.362 --> 01:01:30.489
- I can't lie to you.
- Those 12,000...

666
01:01:30.598 --> 01:01:34.694
What are we supposed to do
with 12,000 francs?

667
01:01:35.369 --> 01:01:36.836
I really don't know.

668
01:01:36.937 --> 01:01:40.338
Maybe betterto keep that money
in your account.

669
01:01:40.441 --> 01:01:42.204
You must know

670
01:01:42.310 --> 01:01:45.871
it can't be withdrawn quickly
if times get tough.

671
01:01:45.980 --> 01:01:47.174
That's just it.

672
01:01:47.281 --> 01:01:50.978
We're holding that money
in case times get tough.

673
01:01:51.185 --> 01:01:53.415
It's getting a little absurd.

674
01:01:53.521 --> 01:01:56.718
I'm getting the impression
this is making you uneasy.

675
01:01:56.824 --> 01:02:00.419
Don't! I'd like to do
something with you.

676
01:02:00.728 --> 01:02:02.787
What are you afraid of?

677
01:02:03.397 --> 01:02:05.797
Nothing... If you want to...

678
01:02:06.901 --> 01:02:10.064
Give him the check
before it's too late.

679
01:02:12.406 --> 01:02:14.340
Or do you prefer cash?

680
01:02:15.309 --> 01:02:17.470
Not for a sum like that.

681
01:02:17.578 --> 01:02:21.070
I'll put it in my account
instead of opening one foryou.

682
01:02:21.182 --> 01:02:22.911
I hope you both realize...

683
01:02:23.017 --> 01:02:26.953
I'm not promising miracles.
Don't expect a gold mine.

684
01:02:27.054 --> 01:02:29.386
That's not what Fred told us.

685
01:02:29.490 --> 01:02:31.720
I'll give you a receipt.

686
01:02:31.826 --> 01:02:33.726
Don't bother, Vincent.

687
01:02:33.828 --> 01:02:36.661
We don't need a receipt from you.

688
01:03:16.237 --> 01:03:18.501
Hey, Dad. You scared me.

689
01:03:18.606 --> 01:03:21.871
- It's late foryou to be out.
- It's OK.

690
01:03:22.943 --> 01:03:25.468
It's cool!
Take me for a ride?

691
01:03:25.746 --> 01:03:27.008
I'm dead tired.

692
01:03:29.984 --> 01:03:31.246
Just a quick ride.

693
01:03:31.352 --> 01:03:33.445
It's really late.

694
01:03:33.921 --> 01:03:35.821
Your mother must be worried.

695
01:03:35.923 --> 01:03:36.890
She knows.

696
01:03:36.991 --> 01:03:39.255
I was at a friend's.
She trusts me.

697
01:03:39.360 --> 01:03:42.386
But I don't want
you running around at night.

698
01:03:42.496 --> 01:03:43.656
That's that.

699
01:04:04.051 --> 01:04:06.849
- Good night, Julien.
- Good night.

700
01:05:22.763 --> 01:05:24.663
Are you coming to bed?

701
01:05:25.399 --> 01:05:26.661
I'm not sleepy.

702
01:05:28.569 --> 01:05:31.265
And I didn't want to wake you.

703
01:05:40.047 --> 01:05:43.574
Things aren't going the way
I had hoped.

704
01:05:45.185 --> 01:05:48.120
I knew it would take time
to adapt.

705
01:05:48.789 --> 01:05:51.019
I didn't think
it would be this hard.

706
01:05:51.125 --> 01:05:53.559
You only started a few weeks ago.

707
01:05:53.661 --> 01:05:57.028
Doesn't it take some time
to get on the right track?

708
01:05:57.131 --> 01:05:58.758
Don't you think so?

709
01:05:59.800 --> 01:06:03.497
I get along well
with my colleagues.

710
01:06:04.505 --> 01:06:06.666
They're easy to talk to.

711
01:06:07.575 --> 01:06:09.167
Good atmosphere.

712
01:06:17.084 --> 01:06:18.779
But still perverse.

713
01:06:20.788 --> 01:06:22.847
That makes lying easy,

714
01:06:23.691 --> 01:06:26.216
tell myself everything's fine.

715
01:06:27.494 --> 01:06:28.688
That's a lie.

716
01:06:36.103 --> 01:06:38.003
I'm afraid I'll disappoint.

717
01:06:38.105 --> 01:06:39.436
Afraid of what?

718
01:06:40.674 --> 01:06:42.665
Afraid I'll disappoint.

719
01:06:44.979 --> 01:06:47.470
Afraid I won't make the grade.

720
01:06:47.581 --> 01:06:52.211
You've had these worries before,
but you always pull through.

721
01:06:52.453 --> 01:06:55.081
I can't handle anything right now.

722
01:06:55.189 --> 01:06:57.214
I'm just going along.

723
01:07:00.527 --> 01:07:03.985
Sometimes I don't even know
what I'm supposed to do.

724
01:07:04.098 --> 01:07:06.464
Nor what's expected of me.

725
01:07:08.168 --> 01:07:09.897
So I start to panic.

726
01:07:11.672 --> 01:07:14.766
A simple phone call
becomes overwhelming.

727
01:07:21.248 --> 01:07:23.682
I go from meeting to meeting.

728
01:07:23.784 --> 01:07:27.720
No time to sum things up
ortake a step back.

729
01:07:32.226 --> 01:07:34.194
I can't think anymore.

730
01:07:35.262 --> 01:07:36.854
My mind is blank.

731
01:07:43.270 --> 01:07:45.329
I look around me,

732
01:07:47.675 --> 01:07:49.973
at the people I work with.

733
01:07:51.445 --> 01:07:54.312
I only see totally unknown faces.

734
01:07:56.350 --> 01:07:58.716
Like moments of absence...

735
01:08:07.061 --> 01:08:09.359
Sorry. I'm just tired.

736
01:08:48.836 --> 01:08:49.928
Hello.

737
01:08:51.505 --> 01:08:53.666
I didn't want to wake you.

738
01:08:54.808 --> 01:08:57.038
It's OK.
ljust dozed off.

739
01:09:00.481 --> 01:09:02.711
I worked late last night.

740
01:09:06.453 --> 01:09:07.715
Can we talk?

741
01:09:09.089 --> 01:09:10.283
Sure, go ahead.

742
01:09:11.992 --> 01:09:14.153
- Thanks, Fati.
-You're welcome.

743
01:09:15.462 --> 01:09:17.521
So tell me about it...

744
01:09:18.031 --> 01:09:19.726
How does it work?

745
01:09:20.534 --> 01:09:22.229
I'm in contact

746
01:09:22.336 --> 01:09:25.396
with a small bank,
via a colleague.

747
01:09:25.739 --> 01:09:28.469
It handles Russian investments.

748
01:09:30.644 --> 01:09:32.635
That makes me nervous.

749
01:09:34.281 --> 01:09:36.181
Isn't that risky?

750
01:09:36.884 --> 01:09:39.375
Investment in emerging markets?

751
01:09:39.486 --> 01:09:41.784
That makes it interesting.

752
01:09:41.889 --> 01:09:45.848
400% gains on the Moscow market
of 1998...

753
01:09:45.959 --> 01:09:48.154
Can't find that anywhere else.

754
01:09:48.262 --> 01:09:49.991
That's one way to look at it.

755
01:09:50.097 --> 01:09:52.531
But don't forget:

756
01:09:52.633 --> 01:09:54.863
the same market, that same year...

757
01:09:54.968 --> 01:09:58.836
Iost 200% of its value
in a single day.

758
01:09:59.173 --> 01:10:02.074
I never said there weren't risks.

759
01:10:05.679 --> 01:10:07.112
I don't know...

760
01:10:08.582 --> 01:10:12.177
You're more convincing
with yourfriends.

761
01:10:12.953 --> 01:10:15.649
I don't know...
It's you who wanted to see me.

762
01:10:15.756 --> 01:10:18.247
I didn't mean to offend you.

763
01:10:22.696 --> 01:10:24.596
Sorry, really sorry...

764
01:10:25.799 --> 01:10:28.233
Your story just isn't clear.

765
01:10:33.207 --> 01:10:35.903
Excuse me. I'll be right back.

766
01:10:36.276 --> 01:10:39.837
- Is something wrong?
- I'll be right back.

767
01:11:17.084 --> 01:11:19.348
I'll take care of it.
Don't worry.

768
01:11:19.453 --> 01:11:20.579
Excuse me...

769
01:11:21.321 --> 01:11:24.188
- Feeling better?
-Yes, I'm fine.

770
01:11:24.291 --> 01:11:25.485
Have a seat.

771
01:11:29.897 --> 01:11:32.092
I think we've met before!

772
01:11:34.101 --> 01:11:35.159
Maybe.

773
01:11:35.269 --> 01:11:38.204
Definitely.
You slept in the parking lot.

774
01:11:38.305 --> 01:11:40.102
I kicked him out before.

775
01:11:40.207 --> 01:11:41.868
I think you're mistaken.

776
01:11:41.975 --> 01:11:44.307
I don't make mistakes.
I memorize faces.

777
01:11:44.411 --> 01:11:47.141
It's OK, Stan.
I'm talking with the gentleman.

778
01:11:47.247 --> 01:11:48.737
OK, Jean-Michel.

779
01:11:52.986 --> 01:11:54.886
Want something else?

780
01:11:55.122 --> 01:11:56.555
The same thing.

781
01:11:57.357 --> 01:11:59.723
Fati! Two coffees, please.

782
01:12:09.002 --> 01:12:10.902
I started to get suspicious.

783
01:12:11.004 --> 01:12:14.440
That last time
when you were with friends...

784
01:12:14.541 --> 01:12:17.032
I thought it was weird.

785
01:12:17.611 --> 01:12:21.240
You didn't seem to believe
what you were saying.

786
01:12:24.885 --> 01:12:27.285
What's true in your story?

787
01:12:27.487 --> 01:12:28.681
Anything?

788
01:12:30.324 --> 01:12:32.884
I don't know.
I don't know you.

789
01:12:33.927 --> 01:12:36.862
Let's start from the beginning...

790
01:12:38.198 --> 01:12:40.291
You aren't working in Switzerland?

791
01:12:41.034 --> 01:12:43.730
I've been out of work for about...

792
01:12:43.837 --> 01:12:47.068
three months, three and a half...

793
01:12:48.308 --> 01:12:51.505
- Collecting unemployment?
- Not even.

794
01:12:51.945 --> 01:12:54.778
I haven't gotten around to that.

795
01:12:55.148 --> 01:12:56.775
My wife doesn't know.

796
01:12:57.217 --> 01:12:59.310
None of my family knows.

797
01:13:01.488 --> 01:13:05.254
What about the money
yourfriends give you?

798
01:13:05.792 --> 01:13:07.623
Hold on!

799
01:13:08.929 --> 01:13:10.658
We're just talking.

800
01:13:10.797 --> 01:13:13.527
You seem like a good guy.
I'm not a cop.

801
01:13:16.203 --> 01:13:19.639
You can't really think
that your story can last?

802
01:13:20.007 --> 01:13:23.101
One day yourfriends
will want their money.

803
01:13:23.210 --> 01:13:25.405
Six months, maybe a year.

804
01:13:25.912 --> 01:13:27.937
What will you do then?

805
01:13:29.216 --> 01:13:32.310
I know it won't last long.
I know...

806
01:13:34.087 --> 01:13:37.079
I'm just buying time.

807
01:13:38.225 --> 01:13:39.283
For now...

808
01:13:39.426 --> 01:13:41.519
You're out of your mind.

809
01:13:43.964 --> 01:13:48.867
Aside from the ones I've seen,
how many have you convinced?

810
01:13:48.969 --> 01:13:50.903
It's getting up there.

811
01:13:52.105 --> 01:13:54.665
I'm in touch with
about a dozen persons.

812
01:13:55.008 --> 01:13:56.805
All friends of yours?

813
01:13:56.977 --> 01:13:58.376
More or less.

814
01:13:59.880 --> 01:14:01.177
Acquaintances.

815
01:14:06.753 --> 01:14:09.813
So what to do now?

816
01:14:21.802 --> 01:14:22.962
Hi, Sylvie.

817
01:14:41.221 --> 01:14:42.381
Come in.

818
01:14:42.489 --> 01:14:44.423
Don't leave the door open.

819
01:14:44.524 --> 01:14:46.424
Doors should be open or closed.

820
01:14:46.560 --> 01:14:49.393
I like that one closed.

821
01:14:58.338 --> 01:14:59.999
Have a seat. Relax.

822
01:15:15.188 --> 01:15:17.019
See this watch?

823
01:15:17.891 --> 01:15:19.825
15,000 francs in France.

824
01:15:20.994 --> 01:15:23.462
I pay 200 in Poland.

825
01:15:24.397 --> 01:15:26.160
I resell them for 1,000.

826
01:15:26.333 --> 01:15:28.460
Minimum quantities of 100.

827
01:15:29.636 --> 01:15:33.094
Farfrom the 200% risks

828
01:15:33.874 --> 01:15:35.501
of emerging markets.

829
01:15:38.445 --> 01:15:39.412
Watches...

830
01:15:40.614 --> 01:15:41.581
Scarves...

831
01:15:43.416 --> 01:15:44.508
T-shirts...

832
01:15:45.352 --> 01:15:47.217
A little bulky,

833
01:15:47.554 --> 01:15:49.215
but they sell well.

834
01:15:51.224 --> 01:15:52.191
Pens...

835
01:15:55.328 --> 01:15:56.420
Sunglasses...

836
01:15:59.900 --> 01:16:02.334
All that makes a lot of money.

837
01:16:03.103 --> 01:16:05.901
That's why your Swiss story
interested me.

838
01:16:06.439 --> 01:16:09.704
Stan gives me a hand,
but that's not enough.

839
01:16:09.976 --> 01:16:11.773
What I'm offering you

840
01:16:11.878 --> 01:16:14.745
is a place in my organization.

841
01:16:15.315 --> 01:16:19.012
Modest, but lucrative,
as you can imagine.

842
01:16:20.053 --> 01:16:22.351
I don't think I'm interested.

843
01:16:24.691 --> 01:16:28.092
You don't seem
to have many options.

844
01:18:13.333 --> 01:18:16.200
Have you heard of
training for development?

845
01:18:16.303 --> 01:18:18.430
Leave out the terminology!

846
01:18:18.905 --> 01:18:21.339
Quiet down,
or it's off to bed!

847
01:18:21.441 --> 01:18:24.467
No stories!
Play quietly, OK?

848
01:18:24.644 --> 01:18:26.305
You're wrong, Dad.

849
01:18:26.446 --> 01:18:30.712
I'll agree that training for development
sounds a little pompous.

850
01:18:30.850 --> 01:18:32.750
But it's no empty term.

851
01:18:32.886 --> 01:18:35.446
I was really surprised to see

852
01:18:35.555 --> 01:18:38.183
that the UN-NGO committee

853
01:18:38.291 --> 01:18:40.759
uses only six UN representatives

854
01:18:40.860 --> 01:18:42.191
out of 26 persons.

855
01:18:42.295 --> 01:18:44.729
The other 20 persons
are NGO members.

856
01:18:44.831 --> 01:18:49.564
So those in the field
are teaching us about local situations.

857
01:18:49.703 --> 01:18:52.228
I know all about those outfits.

858
01:18:52.806 --> 01:18:56.139
It's mostly about
never-ending meetings

859
01:18:56.209 --> 01:18:58.040
without any results!

860
01:18:58.678 --> 01:19:01.238
For example,
what decisions are made?

861
01:19:01.348 --> 01:19:05.614
Simply put, we help create companies
in developing countries.

862
01:19:05.785 --> 01:19:08.549
It's a little more complicated
than that.

863
01:19:08.655 --> 01:19:12.284
We offerfinancing
to start up the company,

864
01:19:12.392 --> 01:19:16.328
but we also follow up
as executive consultants.

865
01:19:16.429 --> 01:19:19.592
Are you dreaming?
Consulting in Africa!

866
01:19:19.666 --> 01:19:21.463
How can you believe in that?

867
01:19:21.601 --> 01:19:23.694
I see it in action.

868
01:19:24.938 --> 01:19:28.032
What's really interesting,
is your specific task...

869
01:19:28.141 --> 01:19:29.836
That fairtrade stuff.

870
01:19:29.943 --> 01:19:33.538
- That's used for coffee.
- Don't believe it...

871
01:19:33.713 --> 01:19:35.044
That's nonsense!

872
01:19:35.215 --> 01:19:37.945
All these small private initiatives

873
01:19:38.084 --> 01:19:41.349
never solved the problems
of under-developed nations.

874
01:19:41.454 --> 01:19:45.288
We all know there's no global answer
to the problem.

875
01:19:45.692 --> 01:19:47.557
- I know, Muriel.
-Just forget it!

876
01:19:47.660 --> 01:19:50.458
It's important
to attempt these efforts.

877
01:19:50.563 --> 01:19:53.657
It's good that Vincent is involved.

878
01:19:53.767 --> 01:19:56.361
But it won't change the world.

879
01:19:56.469 --> 01:19:58.403
Typical remark of an old ass!

880
01:19:58.505 --> 01:19:59.904
Be nice, Vincent.

881
01:20:00.673 --> 01:20:02.573
You're silly.
I'm not attacking you.

882
01:20:03.009 --> 01:20:06.308
If anyone is happy foryour post,
it's me.

883
01:20:08.114 --> 01:20:12.050
But if we can't even
talk about your job anymore...

884
01:20:12.152 --> 01:20:14.916
Stop it. That's enough!
It's time for bed.

885
01:20:15.021 --> 01:20:16.921
Get to bed.

886
01:20:17.023 --> 01:20:19.787
Tonight you're going to bed early.

887
01:20:20.059 --> 01:20:21.651
Good night, kids.

888
01:20:25.999 --> 01:20:28.991
-Another kiss, Mom!
- Go to sleep!

889
01:20:29.135 --> 01:20:31.968
Are you all settled
in your apartment?

890
01:20:32.138 --> 01:20:35.539
Not much decor,
but it's real comfortable.

891
01:20:36.576 --> 01:20:39.773
Lots of light?

892
01:20:40.113 --> 01:20:41.546
Yes, it's real nice.

893
01:20:41.815 --> 01:20:45.842
But I'm mostly there at night.

894
01:20:46.052 --> 01:20:49.818
There's a view of the lake
if I stretch my neck far enough.

895
01:20:50.690 --> 01:20:52.783
Do you cook when you're alone?

896
01:20:53.193 --> 01:20:55.491
I usually just order pizzas.

897
01:20:56.095 --> 01:20:58.655
I never invite anyone over,

898
01:20:59.466 --> 01:21:03.493
so the kitchen isn't fully equipped.

899
01:21:03.603 --> 01:21:06.401
Only a coffee makerforthe mornings.

900
01:21:06.606 --> 01:21:08.335
Just like a bachelor!

901
01:21:08.575 --> 01:21:10.702
We could go and visit you,

902
01:21:10.877 --> 01:21:12.105
if you'd like.

903
01:21:12.312 --> 01:21:14.906
But Geneva isn't very beautiful.

904
01:21:15.048 --> 01:21:16.948
We already know Geneva!

905
01:21:17.083 --> 01:21:19.347
We're not interested in the city.

906
01:21:19.452 --> 01:21:21.511
We want to see your apartment,

907
01:21:21.621 --> 01:21:23.589
see how you're living.

908
01:21:23.857 --> 01:21:24.881
Whateveryou want...

909
01:21:24.991 --> 01:21:28.518
After all the money
I put into that apartment,

910
01:21:28.628 --> 01:21:30.858
I think I have the right to visit!

911
01:21:30.964 --> 01:21:32.454
Don't start!

912
01:21:32.565 --> 01:21:35.932
It cost me to get settled in
and I had to change cars.

913
01:21:36.035 --> 01:21:38.503
But I can start paying you back
next month.

914
01:21:38.605 --> 01:21:41.369
That's not what yourfather meant.

915
01:21:41.441 --> 01:21:45.172
We'd just like to go
and spend a day with you.

916
01:21:46.012 --> 01:21:49.140
Vincent promised to take me soon.
I'll tell you about it.

917
01:21:49.449 --> 01:21:50.541
That's nice.

918
01:21:50.650 --> 01:21:52.811
Just the two of you together,

919
01:21:52.919 --> 01:21:54.181
without the kids!

920
01:21:54.287 --> 01:21:56.312
That will do us some good.

921
01:21:57.290 --> 01:21:59.019
I'll go and kiss the kids.

922
01:22:00.693 --> 01:22:03.287
They're probably already asleep.

923
01:22:31.291 --> 01:22:33.259
What are you doing, Dad?

924
01:22:38.798 --> 01:22:39.765
Dad?

925
01:23:24.677 --> 01:23:26.645
The border is coming up.

926
01:23:27.914 --> 01:23:29.006
Drive slowly.

927
01:23:30.984 --> 01:23:33.509
The road isn't cleared of snow.

928
01:23:46.532 --> 01:23:48.659
You're so focused!

929
01:23:51.270 --> 01:23:52.965
I love to drive.

930
01:23:56.809 --> 01:23:59.209
When I first started working,

931
01:23:59.746 --> 01:24:02.112
driving was my favorite part.

932
01:24:05.151 --> 01:24:07.745
Alone in the car...

933
01:24:09.455 --> 01:24:11.480
Thinking about nothing...

934
01:24:13.059 --> 01:24:15.857
Smoking and listening to music...

935
01:24:19.632 --> 01:24:21.600
I could go on for hours.

936
01:24:26.039 --> 01:24:29.975
I think the only thing
I really liked about my job

937
01:24:30.610 --> 01:24:32.043
was the driving.

938
01:24:37.550 --> 01:24:40.246
That ended up working against me.

939
01:24:41.354 --> 01:24:45.586
It felt so good in my car,
I had difficulty leaving it.

940
01:24:48.061 --> 01:24:51.155
Sometimes I'd drive 200 km
for an appointment.

941
01:24:53.166 --> 01:24:56.966
Without thinking,
I'd miss the turnoff.

942
01:24:58.638 --> 01:25:00.401
I'd just keep driving.

943
01:25:02.742 --> 01:25:05.677
My boss started to get annoyed,

944
01:25:07.246 --> 01:25:10.306
but things could have been worse.

945
01:25:11.884 --> 01:25:14.352
They felt I no longer
had the company spirit.

946
01:25:14.454 --> 01:25:16.319
No one tried to keep me.

947
01:25:16.422 --> 01:25:18.390
Negotiating my departure
was easy.

948
01:25:20.460 --> 01:25:22.826
Why didn't you tell your wife?

949
01:25:26.365 --> 01:25:27.696
I don't know...

950
01:25:28.835 --> 01:25:31.998
Maybe it was just easier
to keep going.

951
01:26:56.389 --> 01:26:58.789
Three boxes fortomorrow.

952
01:26:58.991 --> 01:27:00.515
Not before 11:00.

953
01:27:00.626 --> 01:27:01.820
I'm tired.

954
01:27:02.762 --> 01:27:04.491
I'll get the otherthree.

955
01:27:06.032 --> 01:27:07.727
300 watches!

956
01:27:09.502 --> 01:27:10.730
Not bad!

957
01:27:16.475 --> 01:27:19.103
We'll straighten up later.

958
01:27:19.212 --> 01:27:21.180
Let's get a bite to eat.

959
01:27:48.140 --> 01:27:49.835
-Are you OK?
- I'm fine.

960
01:27:50.142 --> 01:27:52.906
I was afraid
you wouldn't be here.

961
01:28:02.922 --> 01:28:04.753
What about your apartment?

962
01:28:05.725 --> 01:28:08.159
We're not headed forthe city.

963
01:28:16.502 --> 01:28:18.060
What are you up to?

964
01:28:18.671 --> 01:28:19.763
Patience...

965
01:28:20.873 --> 01:28:24.673
- I've got a surprise.
- Now I'm really scared!

966
01:28:35.721 --> 01:28:37.848
What's all that for?

967
01:28:37.957 --> 01:28:40.391
A short hike in the mountains.

968
01:28:40.826 --> 01:28:43.420
I see you've planned everything.

969
01:29:25.271 --> 01:29:28.206
- Don't exaggerate.
- It's cold!

970
01:29:28.307 --> 01:29:31.003
This way, I can judge everything.

971
01:29:31.277 --> 01:29:32.767
The whole truth...

972
01:29:36.549 --> 01:29:37.880
Now...

973
01:29:38.818 --> 01:29:42.276
The feet, the legs... OK.

974
01:29:42.989 --> 01:29:46.288
Too bad you've lost some
of those nice thighs!

975
01:29:46.993 --> 01:29:47.982
That...

976
01:29:48.928 --> 01:29:50.657
- OK.
-Whew!

977
01:29:51.364 --> 01:29:54.993
Getting a little thicker up here,
but I like it.

978
01:29:55.067 --> 01:29:57.228
There's something that bugs me.

979
01:29:57.336 --> 01:29:59.668
- Stomach?
- No, not that.

980
01:30:00.039 --> 01:30:02.507
The tits are starting to fall.

981
01:30:02.608 --> 01:30:04.269
You're so hard!

982
01:30:04.377 --> 01:30:08.040
Mine are falling, too.
Why should you be spared?

983
01:30:15.388 --> 01:30:18.323
Will we see your apartment
tomorrow?

984
01:30:22.161 --> 01:30:23.719
You really want to?

985
01:30:25.097 --> 01:30:27.327
That's the reason I came!

986
01:30:27.433 --> 01:30:29.628
But it's not an obligation.

987
01:30:30.536 --> 01:30:33.130
You don't seem like you want to.

988
01:30:37.176 --> 01:30:38.507
What's going on?

989
01:30:40.046 --> 01:30:42.412
Is your job getting you down?

990
01:30:43.215 --> 01:30:46.844
I want you to tell me
if something is bothering you.

991
01:30:47.153 --> 01:30:48.643
No, it's not that.

992
01:30:50.156 --> 01:30:53.125
I want to be with you,
away from all that.

993
01:30:54.126 --> 01:30:56.560
The apartment isn't important.

994
01:30:57.596 --> 01:30:59.427
What's not right in Geneva?

995
01:30:59.532 --> 01:31:01.090
Everything is fine.

996
01:31:02.134 --> 01:31:03.931
Why not talk about it?

997
01:32:02.194 --> 01:32:03.161
Are you OK?

998
01:32:03.662 --> 01:32:05.027
Yeah, I'm fine.

999
01:34:08.854 --> 01:34:11.152
Did you think you'd lost me?

1000
01:34:25.904 --> 01:34:29.237
You have to admit it's strange.
Try to understand Philippe.

1001
01:34:29.441 --> 01:34:33.138
We gave the money months ago
and hardly any news.

1002
01:34:33.279 --> 01:34:35.179
I did keep you updated.

1003
01:34:35.881 --> 01:34:38.076
What did he expect
aftertwo months?

1004
01:34:38.150 --> 01:34:41.642
He gave you 150,000 francs.

1005
01:34:41.754 --> 01:34:44.086
He has the right
to ask questions.

1006
01:34:44.189 --> 01:34:45.986
I answered your questions.

1007
01:34:46.091 --> 01:34:48.719
I gave you updates on the values.

1008
01:34:49.261 --> 01:34:51.126
What more does he want?

1009
01:34:51.830 --> 01:34:55.425
He was hoping to be
in direct contact with the bank.

1010
01:34:55.567 --> 01:34:57.262
That would be more practical.

1011
01:34:57.369 --> 01:35:00.395
- Does he want the number?
-Yeah, I think so.

1012
01:35:00.506 --> 01:35:03.634
We can't call the bank,
especially not from France.

1013
01:35:05.044 --> 01:35:07.808
I called you
for some information.

1014
01:35:07.913 --> 01:35:11.542
I have to tell you,
I'm perplexed.

1015
01:35:13.018 --> 01:35:15.714
So Philippe wants his money back?

1016
01:35:15.821 --> 01:35:17.448
Admit that you're vague.

1017
01:35:17.523 --> 01:35:20.686
No problem, I'll reimburse him!

1018
01:35:20.793 --> 01:35:22.988
I don't think you understand.

1019
01:35:23.095 --> 01:35:24.790
He won't be the only one.

1020
01:35:24.897 --> 01:35:29.231
I understand perfectly well.
You're the one who's suspicious.

1021
01:35:29.335 --> 01:35:32.964
I have no problem giving you both
your money back!

1022
01:35:33.605 --> 01:35:35.664
This is really upsetting.

1023
01:35:36.308 --> 01:35:38.333
I don't know what to say.

1024
01:35:40.479 --> 01:35:42.447
I don't know what to think.

1025
01:35:42.581 --> 01:35:45.175
I don't know what to say either.

1026
01:35:52.991 --> 01:35:55.824
I never knew
we'd make so much money!

1027
01:35:55.928 --> 01:35:59.125
Take your share.
It's the end of the month.

1028
01:36:03.268 --> 01:36:04.895
How much did we say?

1029
01:36:05.003 --> 01:36:07.631
You know it's 40,000!

1030
01:36:15.080 --> 01:36:17.844
Would you mind
giving me an advance?

1031
01:36:17.983 --> 01:36:19.314
How much?

1032
01:36:20.252 --> 01:36:21.378
Double.

1033
01:36:22.421 --> 01:36:23.388
Wow!

1034
01:36:23.756 --> 01:36:25.587
You're not shy!

1035
01:36:27.526 --> 01:36:30.393
What's happening?
Paying yourfriends back?

1036
01:36:31.463 --> 01:36:32.794
Yeah, that's it.

1037
01:36:33.499 --> 01:36:34.693
Well, go on.

1038
01:36:55.487 --> 01:36:57.045
What's this?

1039
01:36:57.623 --> 01:36:58.590
What?

1040
01:36:58.824 --> 01:37:00.451
The orange notebook?

1041
01:37:01.226 --> 01:37:02.750
My biography.

1042
01:37:03.095 --> 01:37:05.529
Read it.
I have nothing to hide.

1043
01:37:18.043 --> 01:37:20.341
So you worked in public relations?

1044
01:37:20.446 --> 01:37:21.640
For a while.

1045
01:37:22.281 --> 01:37:24.613
I had a friend in politics.

1046
01:37:26.218 --> 01:37:28.118
His party needed money.

1047
01:37:29.121 --> 01:37:30.418
And so did I!

1048
01:37:31.056 --> 01:37:32.717
We schemed around together.

1049
01:37:34.927 --> 01:37:38.021
I was stupid, a little naive.

1050
01:37:39.097 --> 01:37:41.258
I took a bit of dough on the way.

1051
01:37:41.366 --> 01:37:43.197
Afine of 1,500,000 francs!

1052
01:37:43.302 --> 01:37:44.269
Yes.

1053
01:37:44.770 --> 01:37:46.795
And locked up for a year.

1054
01:37:47.673 --> 01:37:49.698
But I shouldn't complain.

1055
01:37:50.642 --> 01:37:53.634
My daughter Annie
made this notebook.

1056
01:37:56.949 --> 01:37:59.076
She calls it my press book.

1057
01:38:00.352 --> 01:38:02.343
She pasted and noted

1058
01:38:03.121 --> 01:38:04.645
the whole story.

1059
01:38:05.591 --> 01:38:07.821
She did a real good job.

1060
01:38:08.694 --> 01:38:10.662
I didn't know you had a daughter.

1061
01:38:10.729 --> 01:38:12.287
She's 19 years old.

1062
01:38:13.499 --> 01:38:15.763
I don't see her much anymore.

1063
01:38:16.134 --> 01:38:18.659
I get the impression
she liked me better

1064
01:38:18.770 --> 01:38:21.204
when I was in prison.

1065
01:38:22.941 --> 01:38:25.774
Must be strange
to lose everything

1066
01:38:25.878 --> 01:38:27.743
from one day to the next.

1067
01:38:29.681 --> 01:38:30.909
Sure.

1068
01:38:32.851 --> 01:38:35.046
I don't feel any worse today.

1069
01:38:36.321 --> 01:38:38.312
It was hard at first.

1070
01:38:39.525 --> 01:38:40.583
But now,

1071
01:38:41.260 --> 01:38:43.854
I feel free of all that.

1072
01:38:53.372 --> 01:38:54.066
Today I'm only taking
what I can sell.

1073
01:38:55.908 --> 01:38:59.071
Last time, 25% was defective.

1074
01:38:59.177 --> 01:39:01.202
Don't make me cry!

1075
01:39:01.513 --> 01:39:03.504
Do you want to see the defects?

1076
01:39:03.649 --> 01:39:06.413
You sell enough.
You can afford it.

1077
01:39:08.220 --> 01:39:10.279
In any case,
it's a risky business.

1078
01:39:10.389 --> 01:39:12.254
- So 500 polos...
- Hi, honey.

1079
01:39:13.292 --> 01:39:14.384
How are you?

1080
01:39:19.031 --> 01:39:21.158
I had a good weekend too.

1081
01:39:23.101 --> 01:39:25.331
I felt betterthan ever.

1082
01:39:26.405 --> 01:39:27.702
Hold on, honey.

1083
01:39:27.940 --> 01:39:29.271
Just a second.

1084
01:39:35.914 --> 01:39:36.881
Hello.

1085
01:39:36.982 --> 01:39:38.609
Sure you're alright?

1086
01:39:41.887 --> 01:39:44.185
I promise we'll do it again.

1087
01:39:44.656 --> 01:39:46.783
We'll go back this spring.

1088
01:39:50.295 --> 01:39:53.025
I'm waiting for a meeting.

1089
01:39:53.565 --> 01:39:55.396
As usual, everyone is late.

1090
01:39:55.500 --> 01:39:56.660
Hello, Muriel.

1091
01:39:57.502 --> 01:39:59.834
Just a colleague.
Forget it.

1092
01:39:59.938 --> 01:40:01.565
How are you, Muriel?

1093
01:40:01.907 --> 01:40:05.468
Sure, he knows your name.
I do speak about you.

1094
01:40:06.311 --> 01:40:07.835
I know lots about you.

1095
01:40:07.946 --> 01:40:09.311
Shut up!

1096
01:40:09.915 --> 01:40:12.440
I'd love to meet you sometime.

1097
01:40:13.185 --> 01:40:15.745
She'd like to meet you, too.

1098
01:40:16.288 --> 01:40:18.017
Here's 30,000.

1099
01:40:18.457 --> 01:40:19.856
The rest, later.

1100
01:40:20.325 --> 01:40:22.623
I'll call you latertonight.

1101
01:40:25.063 --> 01:40:27.031
What's going on, Muriel?

1102
01:40:30.402 --> 01:40:32.097
I miss you, too.

1103
01:40:34.072 --> 01:40:35.403
Are you alright?

1104
01:40:37.209 --> 01:40:39.336
You seem a little strange.

1105
01:40:40.579 --> 01:40:41.807
I seem strange?

1106
01:40:43.015 --> 01:40:44.414
I don't think so.

1107
01:40:46.251 --> 01:40:49.414
I've got to go
stop the kids from fighting.

1108
01:40:49.521 --> 01:40:51.318
Time to be the police.

1109
01:40:52.491 --> 01:40:53.822
I love you, too.

1110
01:41:30.929 --> 01:41:33.489
Jeff, I'm transferring a call
to your office.

1111
01:41:33.598 --> 01:41:34.860
Thanks.

1112
01:41:35.967 --> 01:41:38.663
- Take your owed days!
- Easily said.

1113
01:41:45.277 --> 01:41:46.608
Yes, I remember.

1114
01:41:48.413 --> 01:41:49.903
Is Vincent OK?

1115
01:41:50.515 --> 01:41:51.880
I don't know.

1116
01:41:52.484 --> 01:41:53.644
Hold on.

1117
01:42:15.173 --> 01:42:17.368
Daddy! Daddy!

1118
01:42:38.363 --> 01:42:42.163
Why did you choose judo
instead of another discipline,

1119
01:42:42.267 --> 01:42:44.098
like Aikido or Tae Kwon Dwe?

1120
01:42:44.202 --> 01:42:46.602
- Tae Kwon Do!
- Don't make fun of me!

1121
01:42:46.705 --> 01:42:48.229
Those are trendy sports.

1122
01:42:48.340 --> 01:42:50.638
All that interior equilibrium!

1123
01:42:52.077 --> 01:42:55.945
I know what you mean.
You don't like that New Age stuff.

1124
01:42:56.047 --> 01:43:00.006
It's too showy,
like that close combat stuff...

1125
01:43:00.118 --> 01:43:02.348
- I forbid that!
- No need.

1126
01:43:02.521 --> 01:43:05.513
I'm not interested.
Those guys are scary.

1127
01:43:05.624 --> 01:43:08.252
Don't want to be like
Jean-Claude Van Damme?

1128
01:43:08.360 --> 01:43:11.090
Judo takes up
all of Julien's time.

1129
01:43:11.163 --> 01:43:14.098
You can't complain.
I get good grades.

1130
01:43:14.199 --> 01:43:18.295
Be grateful, Vincent.
You have a kid with a passion.

1131
01:43:18.537 --> 01:43:22.633
If I had a kid,
I'd want him to dream about the future.

1132
01:43:23.809 --> 01:43:25.640
What do you do exactly?

1133
01:43:25.744 --> 01:43:28.770
Pardon me?
Sorry, I was still in Aikido.

1134
01:43:30.115 --> 01:43:33.573
I have no idea what you do.
Do you work in his department?

1135
01:43:33.685 --> 01:43:36.245
Vincent rarely brings home colleagues.

1136
01:43:36.354 --> 01:43:38.117
I'll tell you right away,

1137
01:43:38.256 --> 01:43:40.918
I'm lucky enough
not to work with him.

1138
01:43:41.026 --> 01:43:42.687
I'm the lucky one!

1139
01:43:43.695 --> 01:43:46.630
We know each other
because we're on the same floor.

1140
01:43:46.765 --> 01:43:50.394
I work in connection
with the European Commission,

1141
01:43:50.502 --> 01:43:52.493
in their anti-fraud sector.

1142
01:43:52.604 --> 01:43:54.265
You fight drug trafficking?

1143
01:43:54.372 --> 01:43:56.067
You like that idea!

1144
01:43:56.174 --> 01:43:58.734
But I deal with fake goods.

1145
01:43:59.110 --> 01:44:00.737
That's less serious.

1146
01:44:00.846 --> 01:44:04.304
I fight to show how serious it is.

1147
01:44:04.416 --> 01:44:06.179
It's no minor crime.

1148
01:44:06.284 --> 01:44:10.345
If I see Reeboks at half-price,
it makes no difference to me.

1149
01:44:10.455 --> 01:44:13.447
The poor quality
quickly wears out.

1150
01:44:13.558 --> 01:44:14.786
What do you know?

1151
01:44:15.193 --> 01:44:17.923
My friends have fake ones
just as solid as the real thing.

1152
01:44:18.029 --> 01:44:22.261
Your Dad might not know.
But I guarantee you it's shit!

1153
01:44:22.400 --> 01:44:26.097
Three laps around the track,
and the soles wear out!

1154
01:44:26.204 --> 01:44:29.196
Plus, it's illegal.

1155
01:44:29.307 --> 01:44:31.070
That's serious!

1156
01:44:31.710 --> 01:44:33.075
That wouldn't stop me.

1157
01:44:33.178 --> 01:44:37.239
If I knew where to find Reeboks
at half price I'd buy them.

1158
01:44:37.349 --> 01:44:41.718
If you really like sports shoes,
you should go to Italy,

1159
01:44:41.820 --> 01:44:43.515
around Naples.

1160
01:44:43.622 --> 01:44:45.351
Are they specialists?

1161
01:44:45.457 --> 01:44:49.985
Naples specializes in clothes.
T-shirts, sweats...

1162
01:44:50.595 --> 01:44:53.462
Florence would interest you less.

1163
01:44:53.565 --> 01:44:55.692
They handle leather goods.

1164
01:44:55.967 --> 01:44:58.902
Turin is more luxury goods.

1165
01:44:59.004 --> 01:45:02.405
Jewelry, precious metals, watches...

1166
01:45:02.540 --> 01:45:05.600
If you know all that,
then why not stop them?

1167
01:45:05.710 --> 01:45:07.075
It's not that easy.

1168
01:45:07.178 --> 01:45:09.578
We know of 200 factories

1169
01:45:09.714 --> 01:45:13.309
in Tuscany alone
that make imitations.

1170
01:45:13.885 --> 01:45:16.046
Everything's out in the open.

1171
01:45:16.154 --> 01:45:19.021
They also make legal products.

1172
01:45:19.124 --> 01:45:22.491
That's why it's not easy
to distinguish

1173
01:45:22.594 --> 01:45:27.054
between the legal
and parallel economies.

1174
01:45:28.500 --> 01:45:29.728
It's a problem.

1175
01:45:30.769 --> 01:45:32.828
Is something wrong, Muriel?

1176
01:45:37.509 --> 01:45:39.067
I'm fine...

1177
01:45:39.177 --> 01:45:40.667
I felt a little dizzy.

1178
01:45:40.779 --> 01:45:42.542
Do you want to take a rest?

1179
01:45:42.647 --> 01:45:44.774
I'm fine.
I guess I drank too much.

1180
01:45:46.484 --> 01:45:48.349
Want to get some air?

1181
01:45:48.453 --> 01:45:49.977
It's warm in here.

1182
01:45:50.822 --> 01:45:51.914
No, it's OK.

1183
01:45:52.490 --> 01:45:55.288
- I'll go with you.
- Not necessary.

1184
01:46:09.374 --> 01:46:11.137
I spoke to Jeffrey.

1185
01:46:14.045 --> 01:46:15.842
What does he want now?

1186
01:46:17.949 --> 01:46:19.075
We spoke...

1187
01:46:47.112 --> 01:46:48.579
Where's Jean-Michel?

1188
01:46:48.680 --> 01:46:52.207
He had breakfast
and went up for a shower.

1189
01:46:52.851 --> 01:46:55.046
The van is loaded.
You can go.

1190
01:46:58.056 --> 01:47:00.149
Can I have a coffee, Fati?

1191
01:47:00.258 --> 01:47:01.225
Sure.

1192
01:47:29.220 --> 01:47:31.245
Stan, come here!

1193
01:47:40.799 --> 01:47:43.063
What is that asshole doing?

1194
01:47:47.038 --> 01:47:48.062
See yourfriend?

1195
01:47:48.139 --> 01:47:50.266
-What's wrong?
- Take a look!

1196
01:48:01.519 --> 01:48:03.714
What's going on?
Has he flipped?

1197
01:48:08.159 --> 01:48:09.251
Forget it!

1198
01:48:36.654 --> 01:48:38.121
What are you doing here?

1199
01:48:38.223 --> 01:48:40.316
Sorry, I was just passing by.

1200
01:48:40.425 --> 01:48:43.451
You should've phoned.
Come and have a bite with us.

1201
01:48:43.561 --> 01:48:47.224
Sorry, I haven't time.
I'm just dropping this off.

1202
01:48:47.332 --> 01:48:48.458
What is it?

1203
01:48:49.067 --> 01:48:50.159
Surprise...

1204
01:48:52.170 --> 01:48:54.934
Your money with interest.
15,000 francs.

1205
01:48:55.039 --> 01:48:56.438
Why bring it to me now?

1206
01:48:56.541 --> 01:48:59.135
Please don't ask for explanations.

1207
01:48:59.244 --> 01:49:01.405
You can't just leave like that!

1208
01:49:01.513 --> 01:49:03.674
3,000 francs interest
in three months!

1209
01:49:03.781 --> 01:49:04.873
Why stop?

1210
01:49:04.983 --> 01:49:06.541
I have to stop.

1211
01:49:06.651 --> 01:49:08.642
Is something wrong?

1212
01:49:08.753 --> 01:49:10.084
No, don't worry.

1213
01:49:10.522 --> 01:49:13.013
I'm not worried,
but you seem worried.

1214
01:49:13.158 --> 01:49:15.456
I feel a little responsible.

1215
01:49:15.793 --> 01:49:18.421
If it's the money,
it really doesn't matter.

1216
01:49:18.530 --> 01:49:20.498
But you need this money.

1217
01:49:20.565 --> 01:49:23.898
You and Jeanne
can't just let yourselves...

1218
01:49:24.002 --> 01:49:25.902
Be careful with your money.

1219
01:49:26.004 --> 01:49:28.199
What's all this about?

1220
01:49:28.306 --> 01:49:30.604
We're friends, like Fred.

1221
01:49:30.708 --> 01:49:32.198
Tell us what's wrong.

1222
01:49:32.310 --> 01:49:33.800
I'll call you, OK?

1223
01:50:37.642 --> 01:50:38.666
Are you happy?

1224
01:50:38.776 --> 01:50:41.574
- Hi, Vincent.
-You couldn't leave Muriel alone?

1225
01:50:41.679 --> 01:50:43.874
Muriel? She called me.

1226
01:50:44.816 --> 01:50:47.182
-What?
-Yes, she called me.

1227
01:50:49.954 --> 01:50:51.854
Haven't you messed up enough?

1228
01:50:51.923 --> 01:50:52.890
What?

1229
01:50:53.391 --> 01:50:56.360
You're not well.
It's obvious.

1230
01:50:56.527 --> 01:50:58.722
What are you talking about?

1231
01:50:58.830 --> 01:51:00.058
That's just it.

1232
01:51:00.565 --> 01:51:02.260
I'm trying to understand.

1233
01:51:02.367 --> 01:51:03.425
Don't touch me!

1234
01:51:03.534 --> 01:51:04.899
Take it easy!

1235
01:51:05.003 --> 01:51:07.301
Forget about me!
Did you hear?

1236
01:51:07.839 --> 01:51:10.433
You know what?
You're ridiculous!

1237
01:51:11.142 --> 01:51:12.109
You idiot!

1238
01:51:27.258 --> 01:51:28.418
We're not home now.

1239
01:51:28.526 --> 01:51:31.962
Leave us a message
and we'll get back to you.

1240
01:51:32.563 --> 01:51:34.292
Muriel, it's me.

1241
01:51:35.633 --> 01:51:37.601
I've had a really bad day.

1242
01:51:37.735 --> 01:51:41.171
I don't feel well.
I've decided to come home.

1243
01:51:42.040 --> 01:51:43.769
I'm on the road.

1244
01:51:44.342 --> 01:51:47.834
I'll be back around 9:30 or 10:00.

1245
01:51:47.945 --> 01:51:50.140
I hope you'll all be there.

1246
01:51:50.615 --> 01:51:51.582
I love you.

1247
01:52:26.984 --> 01:52:28.781
Daddy's home!

1248
01:52:28.886 --> 01:52:30.513
Hey, little monster.

1249
01:52:41.532 --> 01:52:43.932
How was school?
Was the teacher nice?

1250
01:52:44.068 --> 01:52:45.797
I had a fight with Youssouf.

1251
01:52:45.903 --> 01:52:48.736
-Were you hurt?
- No, he got hurt.

1252
01:52:49.374 --> 01:52:50.602
Hi, Alice.

1253
01:52:51.376 --> 01:52:52.536
How's my girl?

1254
01:52:52.877 --> 01:52:55.311
- Did you have a good day?
-Yes.

1255
01:52:56.681 --> 01:52:59.741
- Mommy's making pasta.
- Really?

1256
01:52:59.884 --> 01:53:01.044
I don't like it.

1257
01:53:01.152 --> 01:53:03.279
You won't make a fuss, will you?

1258
01:53:03.388 --> 01:53:07.415
She always says that,
but then she's happy to eat it.

1259
01:53:09.827 --> 01:53:11.055
Hey, you.

1260
01:53:25.343 --> 01:53:26.571
Where's Julien?

1261
01:53:26.677 --> 01:53:28.440
In his room.

1262
01:53:33.117 --> 01:53:34.084
Julien?

1263
01:53:40.258 --> 01:53:42.385
He'll come down soon.

1264
01:53:42.994 --> 01:53:45.827
Julien, come down now!

1265
01:53:46.164 --> 01:53:47.495
What do you want?

1266
01:53:47.598 --> 01:53:49.725
I'm calling Julien!

1267
01:53:59.544 --> 01:54:01.273
Do you need help, Muriel?

1268
01:54:01.379 --> 01:54:03.643
It's OK.
It's almost ready.

1269
01:54:11.222 --> 01:54:13.190
Your hair's getting long!

1270
01:54:13.291 --> 01:54:14.656
No, it's not!

1271
01:54:14.759 --> 01:54:16.954
Yes, time for a haircut.

1272
01:54:17.061 --> 01:54:18.426
I don't want to go!

1273
01:54:18.529 --> 01:54:20.554
You can't stay like that.

1274
01:54:21.599 --> 01:54:23.328
I can stay like that!

1275
01:54:28.239 --> 01:54:31.800
- Did you fight with your sister?
- No fights.

1276
01:54:32.543 --> 01:54:36.138
I didn't fight, crazy man!

1277
01:54:36.247 --> 01:54:38.477
Talking like that to me,
you're crazy.

1278
01:54:39.283 --> 01:54:41.649
Crazy isn't a bad word.

1279
01:54:42.253 --> 01:54:44.153
But it's not very nice.

1280
01:54:54.732 --> 01:54:56.859
Is Julien coming down?

1281
01:55:03.007 --> 01:55:05.737
Julien, come down!
It's almost ready.

1282
01:55:19.757 --> 01:55:21.122
You're sleepy.

1283
01:55:21.325 --> 01:55:23.418
Julien, come down.
Yourfather's home.

1284
01:55:23.528 --> 01:55:24.790
I don't want to see him.

1285
01:55:24.929 --> 01:55:26.829
Supper's ready.
Come down.

1286
01:55:26.898 --> 01:55:28.627
I'm not hungry.
I don't want to see him.

1287
01:55:28.833 --> 01:55:32.234
- I'm not disturbing anyone!
- Come down.

1288
01:55:32.336 --> 01:55:35.203
I don't want to see him!
Stop insisting.

1289
01:55:35.373 --> 01:55:36.965
What's wrong with him?

1290
01:55:37.074 --> 01:55:39.065
Don't make matters
more complicated.

1291
01:55:39.176 --> 01:55:42.111
I won't eat with him.
He's a bastard!

1292
01:55:42.914 --> 01:55:45.508
You sit and face him!

1293
01:55:46.350 --> 01:55:47.749
He makes me sick!

1294
01:55:47.885 --> 01:55:50.683
- That's enough!
- Leave me alone!

1295
01:55:53.824 --> 01:55:55.815
Why doesn't he want
to come down?

1296
01:55:55.927 --> 01:55:57.861
Leave him, he's not hungry.

1297
01:55:57.962 --> 01:56:00.487
- Let me speak to him.
- Let him be.

1298
01:56:00.631 --> 01:56:03.225
Why? Can't I speak to my son?

1299
01:56:06.571 --> 01:56:07.970
Why so quiet?

1300
01:56:12.877 --> 01:56:14.708
What's wrong with all of you?

1301
01:56:16.080 --> 01:56:17.809
Are you scared of me?

1302
01:56:19.917 --> 01:56:22.044
You're scared, is that it?

1303
01:56:35.833 --> 01:56:36.925
What's wrong?

1304
01:56:37.635 --> 01:56:38.602
Tell me!

1305
01:56:38.736 --> 01:56:40.226
You know what's wrong!

1306
01:56:40.338 --> 01:56:41.396
No, tell me!

1307
01:56:41.772 --> 01:56:42.864
You know...

1308
01:56:42.974 --> 01:56:44.305
You bullshit us!

1309
01:56:46.711 --> 01:56:47.678
What?

1310
01:56:47.812 --> 01:56:49.302
You laughed at us!

1311
01:56:53.150 --> 01:56:54.412
What's wrong?

1312
01:56:56.320 --> 01:56:57.412
Just tell me.

1313
01:57:00.925 --> 01:57:02.324
What's different?

1314
01:57:04.395 --> 01:57:05.953
Was I too absent?

1315
01:57:07.264 --> 01:57:09.698
Didn't I take care
of all of you?

1316
01:57:11.035 --> 01:57:12.024
So...

1317
01:57:12.970 --> 01:57:15.370
That's it...
It took me some time.

1318
01:57:17.241 --> 01:57:20.074
What did you think?
It's not that easy.

1319
01:57:31.322 --> 01:57:34.223
So you think I'm a bastard?

1320
01:57:35.660 --> 01:57:37.958
But nothing changed foryou.

1321
01:57:38.162 --> 01:57:39.959
Are you aware of that?

1322
01:57:40.665 --> 01:57:44.328
I did that so you could live
like nothing happened...

1323
01:57:44.902 --> 01:57:47.029
I could have just run off.

1324
01:57:47.571 --> 01:57:48.868
You know that?

1325
01:57:48.973 --> 01:57:50.531
I could have run off.

1326
01:57:50.641 --> 01:57:51.608
Let him go.

1327
01:57:54.412 --> 01:57:56.312
Let him go.
He's afraid.

1328
01:57:58.282 --> 01:57:59.249
Come on...

1329
01:57:59.950 --> 01:58:01.884
We'll talk, just us.

1330
01:58:05.022 --> 01:58:06.649
Nothing to say.

1331
01:58:06.791 --> 01:58:09.851
What do you think?
I have nothing to say.

1332
01:58:10.127 --> 01:58:12.152
Yourfather is coming by.

1333
01:58:12.296 --> 01:58:13.923
He wants to talk.

1334
01:58:15.266 --> 01:58:17.894
What the hell
is he coming here for?

1335
01:58:18.002 --> 01:58:19.970
Did you ask him to come?

1336
01:58:20.871 --> 01:58:23.237
I don't feel like seeing him.

1337
01:58:48.032 --> 01:58:49.431
I'm really sorry.

1338
01:58:50.835 --> 01:58:52.359
What are you sorry about?

1339
01:58:53.170 --> 01:58:54.569
Stop it, Vincent.

1340
01:59:04.949 --> 01:59:08.180
I don't understand
why he's coming here.

1341
01:59:10.688 --> 01:59:11.916
Nothing to say.

1342
01:59:29.240 --> 01:59:30.969
I'm just tired.

1343
01:59:32.476 --> 01:59:35.070
None of you know
how tired I am.

1344
01:59:36.714 --> 01:59:40.115
I think ljust won't go
to work this week.

1345
01:59:40.618 --> 01:59:41.778
I need a rest.

1346
01:59:52.496 --> 01:59:54.862
What are you all doing there?

1347
01:59:56.367 --> 01:59:59.598
Are you just going to watch me
all night?

1348
02:00:01.305 --> 02:00:03.705
You're all completely sick!

1349
02:01:01.832 --> 02:01:02.958
Vincent?

1350
02:01:05.870 --> 02:01:07.098
Can you hear...

1351
02:01:19.617 --> 02:01:20.777
Don't hang up!

1352
02:01:21.785 --> 02:01:22.945
Where are you?

1353
02:01:24.455 --> 02:01:25.786
It's not serious...

1354
02:01:25.890 --> 02:01:28.586
Money problems can be worked out.

1355
02:01:32.296 --> 02:01:35.356
If you don't want to talk,
we won't talk.

1356
02:01:36.100 --> 02:01:38.933
You don't have to explain anything.

1357
02:01:41.405 --> 02:01:44.169
This will be forgotten in a month.

1358
02:01:44.541 --> 02:01:46.168
We all believe that!

1359
02:01:47.811 --> 02:01:49.745
Just answer us...

1360
02:02:18.342 --> 02:02:19.866
Vincent, it's me.

1361
02:02:20.945 --> 02:02:22.037
Vincent?

1362
02:02:23.981 --> 02:02:26.449
I'm alone.
Just us two.

1363
02:02:26.817 --> 02:02:28.444
Won't you answer me?

1364
02:02:39.863 --> 02:02:40.955
You've stopped?

1365
02:02:41.332 --> 02:02:42.731
What's happening?

1366
02:02:45.803 --> 02:02:47.896
Can't you say something?

1367
02:02:50.941 --> 02:02:53.068
I'm sure you're listening.

1368
02:02:53.444 --> 02:02:56.811
If you're listening,
then you agree to speak to me.

1369
02:02:56.914 --> 02:02:57.881
Right?

1370
02:03:05.656 --> 02:03:07.624
I want to be with you.

1371
02:03:08.392 --> 02:03:09.484
I miss you.

1372
02:03:11.996 --> 02:03:14.191
Don't destroy everything...

1373
02:03:14.898 --> 02:03:17.093
Don't leave me all alone...

1374
02:03:18.802 --> 02:03:20.702
I'm tired, Vincent.

1375
02:03:22.239 --> 02:03:23.206
I love you.

1376
02:03:36.587 --> 02:03:39.055
I was at DR Consulting
forfive years.

1377
02:03:39.156 --> 02:03:41.181
It was a learning experience.

1378
02:03:41.291 --> 02:03:43.486
What position did you hold?

1379
02:03:43.827 --> 02:03:45.920
I was a financial consultant.

1380
02:03:46.030 --> 02:03:49.522
I decided to go to Partner.

1381
02:03:51.068 --> 02:03:54.060
-And you stayed on 11 years?
- Right.

1382
02:03:54.505 --> 02:03:57.668
Eleven years with Partner
is good experience.

1383
02:03:58.108 --> 02:03:59.871
But you decided to leave?

1384
02:03:59.977 --> 02:04:01.171
Can you tell me why?

1385
02:04:01.278 --> 02:04:04.008
I felt like I was
going around in circles.

1386
02:04:04.114 --> 02:04:06.947
I didn't see any new opportunities.

1387
02:04:07.284 --> 02:04:10.515
I'm someone who functions
on enthusiasm.

1388
02:04:10.754 --> 02:04:12.915
You stopped working for seven months!

1389
02:04:13.023 --> 02:04:16.618
What happened?
You hadn't prepared your departure...

1390
02:04:17.928 --> 02:04:20.988
I did a lot of prospecting
in that period.

1391
02:04:21.098 --> 02:04:22.690
I chose to take my time

1392
02:04:22.800 --> 02:04:25.030
and find a job
that would fully satisfy me.

1393
02:04:25.135 --> 02:04:26.261
I understand.

1394
02:04:26.370 --> 02:04:29.806
Knowing how to wait
is a good quality,

1395
02:04:29.907 --> 02:04:33.308
especially after 11 years
with the same company.

1396
02:04:35.045 --> 02:04:36.876
It's important to reflect

1397
02:04:36.980 --> 02:04:41.815
on what we can offer,
and what we expect of a company.

1398
02:04:42.486 --> 02:04:46.217
Yourfather says
you're not short on ambition.

1399
02:04:46.323 --> 02:04:48.450
I think those things are connected.

1400
02:04:48.559 --> 02:04:50.584
Well, that's what he says.

1401
02:04:50.694 --> 02:04:54.027
Ambition is what drives a career.

1402
02:04:54.665 --> 02:04:59.102
We're offering you
a senior position

1403
02:05:00.737 --> 02:05:03.467
in a new area
we've begun to develop.

1404
02:05:03.574 --> 02:05:05.974
We'll invest heavily.

1405
02:05:06.076 --> 02:05:10.877
A strategic financial venture...

1406
02:05:10.981 --> 02:05:15.179
And, at least in our eyes,
a human venture.

1407
02:05:15.886 --> 02:05:18.855
You'll have a team of eight people.

1408
02:05:19.423 --> 02:05:21.618
Ateam you'll have to mold.

1409
02:05:21.925 --> 02:05:24.951
We're offering you many challenges.

1410
02:05:26.763 --> 02:05:30.665
Your personal investment is required.

1411
02:05:31.602 --> 02:05:33.797
That is, if you are chosen.

1412
02:05:34.938 --> 02:05:36.496
To be clear...

1413
02:05:36.940 --> 02:05:40.603
I'm not trying to pressure you.

1414
02:05:41.178 --> 02:05:45.638
ljust won't minimalize yourtask.

1415
02:05:48.352 --> 02:05:49.910
But I'm not scared.

1416
02:05:54.858 --> 02:05:57.918
Then let's go overthe details.

1417
02:08:01.084 --> 02:08:03.279
Adaptation: Richard Lormand
